 (the root) owns the ACCESS_POLICY gate; this validates and stores only.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>ClassId</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Level</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_AccessLevel</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ForWrite</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>n</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_DeclareClass</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8d - declare a data class, normally at Setup on every boot. The levels
 are DEFAULTS: a class already in the persistent table keeps the levels a
 deployment edited, and only its label follows the code. Refused when the
 table is full, the id is empty, or a level is out of range.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>ClassId</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>LabelKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ReadLevel</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_AccessLevel</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>WriteLevel</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_AccessLevel</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>n</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>PermitsLogged</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ gated-entry check: a DENIED attempt is audited as a MESSAGE event (§8.3/§7.7(c))]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Gate</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_GatedAction</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_DataLevel</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8d - the EFFECTIVE level to read or write a value: its class's level,
