 AUTO_RESET come+gone event (§8.3(c)) plus the §3.13 flow-chart row mark.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Diag</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</Type><BitSize>5568</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_SequenceStep</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §6.5/§3.13 — the per-row LIVE state of one flow-chart row: 7 bytes.

 Everything static about a row (its number, leg, time class, guard and text) is in
 ST_SequenceStepDef, served once through the §3.10.2 manifest. Everything about
 which row is running RIGHT NOW is in ST_SequenceCursor, one entry per concurrent
 leg. What is left here is the small set that is per-row AND changes over time,
 and that the HMI could not reconstruct by watching: a poll at a few Hz against a
 task at kHz cannot see a step shorter than its own interval, so a chart that
 accumulated these client-side would silently skip fast steps and lose transient
 errors. The chart shows what the chain DID, not what someone happened to catch.]]></Comment><BitSize>96</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Visited</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ reached at least once since the chain reset]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>LastDuration</Name><Type>TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ how long it ran on its last visit]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ErrorActive</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ §6.9(d)/(e) marks. The text and the drill-down link are in the annotation
 table; these say only that the row has one, which is all the chart needs to
 colour it - so a row stays correctly marked even if that table is full.]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>WarningActive</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>72</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_SequenceStepDef</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §3.13/§3.10.2 — the STATIC definition of a flow-chart row.

 Every field here is fixed from the step's first visit, so none of it belongs in a
 cyclic read. It is served through the config manifest (M_AppendConfig) under the
 SAME browse paths the live row uses, so the HMI reads one row structure and never
 learns that half of it arrived once and was cached.]]></Comment><BitSize>2688</BitSize><SubItem><Name>StepNo</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Branch</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ §6.12 which concurrent leg this step belongs to. 0 = the chain's main line.]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>16</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>TimeClass</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_TimeClass</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ExpectedTime</Name><Type>TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ 0 = no declared guard]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>StepName</Name><Type>STRING(120)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ localization key]]></Comment><BitSize>968</BitSize><BitOffs>96</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>AwaitingLabel</Name><Type>STRING(120)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ e.g. 'PressRam.EXTEND' ('' if none)]]></Comment><BitSize>968</BitSize><BitOffs>1064</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>AwaitsPath</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.13 drill-down target: the Fraktal path of the module this step commands.
 STRING(80) because that is what it is copied from - I_Module.Name, backed by
 FB_ModuleBase._name : STRING(80). A module path cannot be longer than its own
 name, so 255 was reserving 175 bytes per row that could never be used.]]></Comment><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>2032</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_SequenceCursor</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §3.13/§6.12 — which row a concurrent leg is running, and for how long.

 Indexed BY BRANCH, because a leg has exactly one active step by definition: index
 0 is the chain's main line, 1..n are its parallel legs. That is what makes this
 table ~10 entries instead of one per row, and small enough to publish cyclically -
 so the chart is already correct the instant its tab opens, instead of after the
 first on-demand read.]]></Comment><BitSize>96</BitSize><SubItem><Name>RowIdx</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ SequenceSteps index; 0 = this leg has no active step]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Elapsed</Name><Type>TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ how long that row has been running]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>TimedOut</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ it outran its own ExpectedTime (a leg's own guard)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_SequenceAnnotation</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §6.9 — one error or message currently attached to a flow-chart row.

 These are SPARSE: an error is one at a time, and messages last only until their
 step is entered again, so a handful are live at once out of a table of 128 rows.
 Reserving the text on every row cost 633 of the row's 1156 bytes for a case that
 is almost always empty. The row keeps the flag; this carries what it says.]]></Comment><BitSize>1648</BitSize><SubItem><Name>RowIdx</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ SequenceSteps index this belongs to; 0 = free slot]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>IsError</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE = §6.9(d) raise (chain stopped), FALSE = §6.9(e) message]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>16</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Key</Name><Type>STRING(120)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ localization key of the reason/message]]></Comment><BitSize>968</BitSize><BitOffs>24</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SourcePath</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Module the chart drills into; '' = this Unit. STRING(80) for the same reason
 as AwaitsPath: it is a module path, bounded by FB_ModuleBase._name.]]></Comment><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>992</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_LineRole</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §3.8e - which copy of a line's data this controller holds.]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BaseType>DINT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>NONE</Text><Enum>0</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ not set up]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>OWNER</Text><Enum>1</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ the one authoritative, editable copy]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>MIRROR</Text><Enum>2</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ a read-only copy applied whole from the owner]]></Comment></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>qualified_only</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_LineRecord</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §3.8e - one line value as it travels from owner to mirror: the same
