 The set is a PROJECTION of the same deterministic walk that builds the
 §3.10.2 manifest: M_AppendConfig runs exactly as a QUERY_CONFIG would run it,
 and the pager files every capability of the requested ConfigKind as a
 (Scope, WriteKey) record. There is no second enumeration of "what this
 station's configuration consists of" to drift from the first (§1.1 O9).

 Kind selects which of the two kinds of set this is: STATION_CFG for a station
 set (deployment data), PAR_CFG for a model set (one model's recipe data).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>SetName</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Kind</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ConfigKind</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>info</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigSetInfo</Type><BitSize>2016</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>records</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_SequenceRegister</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §6.8 register an attached chain (idempotent, bounded). Called from
 FB_SequenceBase.M_Attach, never by project code.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Seq</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_Sequence</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>WriteModelConfig</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8a - WriteConfig for the model AvailableModels[ModelIndex] (0 = the active
 model). A model-data value is stored in that model's record and saved back to
 the provider; any other value is written as WriteConfig writes it.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>ModelIndex</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>TargetPath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>WriteKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Revision</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>TextValue</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_OpenModelView</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Serve model-scoped values of AvailableModels[Index] for this one request. 0,
 or the active model's index, is the live record and opens nothing. The record
 is loaded over a copy of the live one, so the provider's SchemaVersion check
 compares like with like. FALSE = no such model, or its record did not load.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Index</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_ResetSequenceRows</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.13 — drop the published flow chart so the next mode builds its own.

 The row table is DISCOVERED by visit (§6.5), which is what makes it free to
 author - but discovery has no end: without this the table becomes the union of
 every chain run since boot. After AUTO then HOME the operator would be shown
 AUTO's rows and HOME's together with only some of them live, and the union of
 the press demo's three modes is 29 rows against a bound of 32. A mode is the
 natural boundary: within one mode a re-run keeps its rows, so Visited and
 LastDuration stay meaningful across cycles.

 Bounded by the count actually in use, not by MAX_SEQUENCE_STEPS: clearing rows
 nobody published would cost the whole table on every mode change (§1.1 O10 -
 deterministic scan time).]]></Comment><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>e</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_SequenceStep</Type><BitSize>96</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>x</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_SequenceStepDef</Type><BitSize>2688</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>c</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_SequenceCursor</Type><BitSize>96</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>a</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_SequenceAnnotation</Type><BitSize>1648</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_HeldCyclic</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §7.6.1a — re-assert the latched hold every scan, and drop it when the client
 stops refreshing. The module's own freshness timer stops the motion; this
 stops the ROOT from going on asking for it.]]></Comment><Local><Name>elapsed</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_AddReason</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §7.8 helper — append one non-interlock reason (bounds-checked).]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Report</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">ST_ReleaseReport</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Text</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Reason</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Reason</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Kind</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ReleaseKind</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>ImportConfigSetPiece</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b - take part of a set line. A request carries at most 255 characters
 and an exported line may hold 480, so a longer line arrives as pieces:
 More = TRUE holds this piece and waits for the next; the first piece without
 More completes the line, which is then imported exactly like a whole one.

 Joined by FB_ConfigSetJson.M_Join, which measures first: a line that would
 exceed its width is refused and the import aborted - never truncated. (Not
 CONCAT/LEN: those stop at 255, which is the very limit being crossed.)]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Piece</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>More</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Commit</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>line</Name><Type>STRING(480)</Type><BitSize>3848</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_SequenceFault</Name><Parameter><Name>Reason</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Reason</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>DescriptionKey</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_PushHistory</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §6.9(a) — fixed ring, newest at HistoryHead; never allocates]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>D</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</Type><BitSize>5568</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_LiveCyclic</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b - read the live documents back once, then write all of them again after
 every accepted change: station, line, then each model. TRUE while a document
 is not yet where it belongs, which holds PersistPending for that long.

 One pass rewrites every document rather than tracking which value changed:
 a pass is bounded (2 + MAX_RECIPES documents), and a document written whole
 from the capability walk can never disagree with the machine.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>n</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>kind</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ConfigKind</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>modelIndex</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>started</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>refused</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ the medium's queue was full: ask again next scan]]></Comment><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_SetOpAllowed</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b — the gate every set operation shares: CONFIG_SET (never DATA_WRITE —
 replacing a machine's entire parametrization is not the same decision as
 changing one number), a wired store, and the owning root READY.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>WriteConfig</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8a/§7.7 centralized HMI configuration authority. Concrete overrides never
 need to remember DATA_WRITE or root ownership; they validate only their field.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>TargetPath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>WriteKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Revision</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>TextValue</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_StageConfigWrite</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8e - the staging walk is the write walk, line leg included.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Scope</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>WriteKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Revision</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>TextValue</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RootReady</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_SequenceSetStep</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ I_SequenceHost (§6.7/§6.8) — step record for a separately-compiled chain.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>StepNo</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>StepName</Name><Type>STRING(120)</Type><BitSize>968</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Awaits</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_Module</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>AwaitingLabel</Name><Type>STRING(120)</Type><BitSize>968</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>TimeClass</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_TimeClass</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ExpectedTime</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Branch</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_CascadeMode</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.7 — offer the mode to child Units; a child may reject (graceful)]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Mode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Mode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>iu</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_Unit</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_RaiseMaintenance</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §8.11.4(d)/§8.12 — a Low-severity maintenance event: informs planning, does not
 stop the cycle. Instant come+gone ring entry (the trend data lives in Profiler).]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Reason</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Reason</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Text</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>slot</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_LogDecision</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Domain audit: request, rejection and resolution are closed MESSAGE events.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>EventKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>SourcePath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Option</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>slot</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>textValue</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>sourceValue</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_DecisionCyclic</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §6.11 one-slot resolver. Operator input wins if it is accepted in the same scan
 the timeout expires; _M_HandleHmiRequest runs immediately before this method.]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>_M_HighestSeverity</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §8.13 — derive the tower input from the authoritative active-event table.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Highest</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">E_Severity</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_PartStarted</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.16.3 EVENT_PART_PROCESSING_STARTED — the value-adding sequence begins.]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>ReleaseReportStart</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §7.8 — pure query: the FULL rollup of why Start would be refused right now.
 This is the authoritative machine predicate consumed by Start (no drift).
 Released = TRUE means Start proceeds. Lists mode + access + blocking-alarm,
 control-domain, and concrete mode-entry release reasons. The caller owns the
 bounded report storage; returning this large record by value can overflow a
 TwinCAT task stack when Start consumes the result.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Report</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">ST_ReleaseReport</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_NokCount</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.16.5 - one judged part. NOK extends the series and enters the window as NOK;
 OK ends the series and enters it as OK; REWORK is not counted here at all. On a
 trip the Unit raises one MANUAL_RESET alarm - the release report then refuses
 Start, as for any blocking alarm - and a running Unit finishes the cycle at its
 stop point (§8.11.1) instead of producing the next reject.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>IsNok</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>DeleteConfigSet</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b - remove a named set. Gated exactly like save and load (CONFIG_SET, a
 wired store, the root READY) because removing somebody's commissioned set is
 the same order of decision as replacing it, and audited with the set name.
 A store that has held MAX_CONFIG_SETS names needs this to hold a new one.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>SetName</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_PartEvent</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.16.3 — one canonical part-lifecycle event: instant come+gone MESSAGE ring entry.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Reason</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Reason</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Text</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>slot</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>txt</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_CopySet</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Freeze untrusted storage before validation or a commit pass.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>SetName</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>info</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigSetInfo</Type><BitSize>2016</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>record</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigRecord</Type><BitSize>2720</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_RouteHeld</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §7.6.1a — derive the enabling-device fact from THIS root's §9 safety facet and
 carry it to the owning module through the registered-child walk.

 F_ManualEnable is the single place the fact is derived, so grepping for it
 lists every path by which motion is authorised by an enabling device. Until
 now it had no production caller at all - the capability existed and nothing
 reached it.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>TargetPath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Value</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>enable</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ManualEnableStatus</Type><BitSize>664</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>SetAccessLevel</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §7.7 persistent per-root policy edit. The policy's own ACCESS_POLICY threshold
 is rechecked before any threshold — including itself — can change.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Gate</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_GatedAction</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Level</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_AccessLevel</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>ResetOee</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §8.5.1 — clear accumulators + ring (shift start). Gated: §7.7 DATA_WRITE; audited §8.3.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>auditSlot</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_SequenceStepGate</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Steppable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_AppendInterlocks</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §7.8 — concrete Units override to append the active mode's immediate
 entry/frontier records via PermIntlk.AppendFailed(SourcePath, Report). Future step waits
 stay in CurrentStep/Pending and are not blanket Start conditions. Base: nothing.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Report</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">ST_ReleaseReport</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>SetMode</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.4/§3.7 — FALSE = unsupported (graceful rejection); TRUE = committed or pending]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Mode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Mode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_DataLevelOf</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8d - the effective level to read or write one registered value, from
 what its owning module declared and this root's policy. The root's own
 framework keys (unit.modePolicy.*) are in the built-in class. An unknown key
 resolves to ADMIN: the write path refuses it anyway, and a level check must
 never be the thing that lets an unknown key through.]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_AccessLevel</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>TargetPath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>WriteKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ForWrite</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>grant</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigAccess</Type><BitSize>448</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>minLevel</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_AccessLevel</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>OnModeExit</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.14.4 — called every scan while a mode request is pending and the Unit is BUSY.
 Return 0 = consent to immediate cancel (default); >0 = still stopping gracefully.]]></Comment><ReturnType>DINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>FirstCall</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RequestedMode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Mode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>SetLine</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8e/§8.5.2 - reference the line this root belongs to (owner or mirror, on
 this controller). A Unit references at most one line; 0 detaches it.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>pLine</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" PointerTo="1">FB_LineData</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_StepGate</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.4.2 — the sequence author calls this at each step boundary; returns TRUE when
 the sequence may advance. Steppable (default TRUE) is the PER-STEP stop-point flag:
 a step with Steppable := FALSE runs straight through even in SINGLE_STEP/HOLD_TO_RUN
 (group several motions into one operator step, or a step unsafe to pause mid-way).
 CONTINUOUS: always TRUE. SINGLE_STEP: TRUE once per StepRequest edge (only if
 Steppable). HOLD_TO_RUN: TRUE while held (only if Steppable). Interlocks are
 enforced by the modules regardless (this only paces the sequence).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Steppable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_LiveItemUsed</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Which documents this root keeps: always the station; the line only when this
 root hosts a line it owns (a mirror's values are its owner's); a model when
 model data is kept, every slot on restore and, when writing, every model the
 catalog offers plus any older slot still to be cleared.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Item</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Restoring</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_SequenceComplete</Name></Method><Method><Name>RequestControlPower</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §9.8 remote control-domain request. The acknowledgement is the result of this
 authorization check; it is never reported accepted before POWER_CONTROL runs.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>ControlOn</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_ModelIndexOf</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ AvailableModels index of a model code, 0 when the catalog does not offer it.]]></Comment><ReturnType>UDINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>ModelCode</Name><Type>STRING(64)</Type><BitSize>520</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>__getModuleType</Name><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ModuleType</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>ModuleType</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ModuleType</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>AcknowledgeConfigRestore</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b — an operator of at least ENGINEER level accepts that a configuration
 image was lost. Under BLOCK_UNTIL_ACKNOWLEDGED this is what releases
 START_STOP again; under DEFAULTS_AND_ANNUNCIATE it is what clears the
 standing annunciation.

 The level is checked directly rather than through a gated action, because
 §3.8b names ENGINEER specifically and a station may legitimately have left
 DATA_WRITE or CONFIG_SET open to a lower level. Acknowledging a lost
 commissioning is a different decision from editing a value.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>_M_HostEvent</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §11.6 one owning projection helper; callers supply only event-specific fields.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Kind</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_HostEventKind</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>PartUid</Name><Type>STRING(64)</Type><BitSize>520</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Subject</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Value</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Verdict</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Verdict</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ReasonCode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Reason</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_RejectConfigSet</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b — refuse a set operation, naming the offending record. "One rejection
 aborts the whole load naming the offending (Scope, WriteKey)": a refusal that
 says only "rejected" leaves an engineer diffing two machines by hand.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Scope</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Key</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_ApplySet</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b - replay the set frozen in _loadSnapshot. STAGED and ALL-OR-NOTHING:
 pass 1 validates every record through its owning module's typed handler and
 changes nothing; only if all of them pass does pass 2 apply them. A record
 whose capability no longer exists fails pass 1 like any other and is named.

 Shared by an operator's LoadConfigSet and the start-up restore of the live
 documents. Restoring skips the session's per-value level (§3.8d(e)): those
 values were accepted once already, and replaying them is the machine's act,
 not an operator's. With a model view open the values go to that record.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>SetName</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RecordCount</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Kind</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ConfigKind</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Restoring</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>record</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigRecord</Type><BitSize>2720</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>applied</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>lineBatch</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_PartAborted</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.16.3 EVENT_PART_PROCESSING_ABORTED — the part leaves without a valid result
 (fault, abort, manual removal). Called automatically on Unit ERROR entry.]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>ManualCommandTo</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §7.6.1 — single gated manual-command entry for the HMI. Accepts ONLY when this
 Unit is in MANUAL (§3.4) AND the user holds MANUAL access (§7.7). Routes to the
 target module's ManualCommand (through the command surface — defended, not
 bypassed). Logs every accept/reject as a §8.3 event. Concrete Units override
 _M_RouteManual to map TargetPath -> the child module.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>TargetPath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Value</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>auditSlot</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>CountRework</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §8.11.2 — REWORK verdict counter (see CountGood)]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>SetPartCarrier</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.16.2 — inject the part carrier at the composition root (0 = traceability off).
 Source-agnostic: BY_POSITION local, RFID, DataMatrix, or host, behind I_PartCarrier.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Carrier</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_PartCarrier</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_StageOneRecord</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b — would this record be accepted? The same two-step the write path
 takes: framework-owned keys first, then the recursive walk to the owning
 module. Sharing the writers' own code with Commit := FALSE is what makes
 "staged" mean something: a separate validator could pass a record the write
 path would then refuse, and the load would be half-applied after all.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Record</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigRecord</Type><BitSize>2720</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_ValidateSetShape</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Exact current capability identity/type/revision; no blanket stale migration.
 AnyRevision: a restored document carries the ConfigRev of an earlier run, which
 says nothing about this one; the per-record identity, type and revision still do.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Store</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_ConfigStore</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Info</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigSetInfo</Type><BitSize>2016</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>AnyRevision</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>expectedInfo</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigSetInfo</Type><BitSize>2016</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>expected</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigRecord</Type><BitSize>2720</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>record</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigRecord</Type><BitSize>2720</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>j</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>hits</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>SetConfigPersistence</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b — substitute the durability provider. The shipped LOCAL_RETAIN writer is
 used when nothing is injected, so this exists for a deployment whose
 configuration genuinely lives somewhere else (a file, a database, an MES) —
 not as one more thing every station has to remember to wire (§1.1 O1).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Provider</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_ConfigPersistence</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_ConfigRestored</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b - TRUE once the live documents are back (or there is no medium). Until
 then a configuration write is refused: the restore would replay over it.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>ImportConfigSetLine</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b — take one line of a set's JSON document back in. A header line opens
 a store save, record lines append to it, and Commit closes it.

 Import writes into the STORE, never into the machine. Bringing a document in
 and applying it to the equipment are two decisions, and keeping them apart is
 what lets LoadConfigSet stay staged and all-or-nothing: an imported set is
 validated against THIS machine's capabilities when somebody chooses to load
 it, not silently as it arrives.

 Everything here is untrusted input in the fullest sense - hand-edited, from
 another vendor's tool, from another machine - so the line is parsed into a
 typed record and nothing more is assumed about it (§5.6, §14).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Line</Name><Type>STRING(480)</Type><BitSize>3848</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Commit</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>info</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigSetInfo</Type><BitSize>2016</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>record</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigRecord</Type><BitSize>2720</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_LiveRestoreItem</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b - the medium answered for one document: replay it, or announce why not.
 Nothing there is a first start; nothing there where the medium confirmed a
 write, a document that does not parse or no longer fits this build, or an older
 copy than the one confirmed, is a lost image announced under the document's
 key. The values then stay as they are - the native retained data - and the next
 pass writes them as the new baseline, so the loss is announced once. (A medium
 that could not answer never gets here: _M_LiveCyclic asks again.)]]></Comment><Local><Name>info</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigSetInfo</Type><BitSize>2016</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>key</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>expected</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ConfigKind</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>applied</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_MarkPersistPending</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b — an accepted write is LIVE. This starts the clock on it becoming
 DURABLE, and the root publishes PersistPending until it is. Called from every
 path that accepts a value, so no project and no module type has to remember
 that a write it just made is not yet safe (§1.1 O1).]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>_M_ConfigPersistFailed</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b — the store rejected the write, or the declared window elapsed with it
 still not durable. Pending stays TRUE because the value is STILL not durable;
 Failed says it will not get there on its own.

 Deliberately NOT retried in a loop: a store that cannot write is not fixed by
 asking again every scan, and a retry storm would bury the one annunciation an
 operator needs. The next accepted write re-arms it.]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>RequestLampTest</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §8.13 — remote request is MANUAL-gated and starts only while the Unit is idle.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>_M_SequenceAnnotationClear</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §6.9 — release annotations. RowIdx 0 means "every row" (the ERROR-cleared edge
 drops all error notes at once); otherwise just that row's note of that kind.
 Freed slots are reused before the table grows, so a chain that warns on many
 steps over many cycles does not exhaust it.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>RowIdx</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>IsError</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>e</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_SequenceAnnotation</Type><BitSize>1648</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>SetEngineeringMode</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §7.5.1 — inject the station's commissioning/engineering gate register at
 Setup, the same shape as SetPartCarrier. Wiring it is what makes the §7.5.2
 standing annunciation appear and what arms the §10.5.1 force surface; a Unit
 with no register is a production Unit and both are simply absent.

 Declaring the framework's OWN force gate happens here rather than in the
 project, so a composition root that wires the register cannot forget it
 (§1.1 O1) and cannot arm forcing without also annunciating it.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Mode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">FB_EngineeringMode</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>OnCyclic</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ base first (§3.14.2); then children, one-shot init, mode transition, stall watch]]></Comment><ReturnType>DINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>publishIdx</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>modeIdx</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Mode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>styleIdx</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_RunStyle</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>previousMode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Mode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>modeExitResult</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>highestSeverity</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Severity</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>alarmActive</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>heldReported</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_OwnsModulePath</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Module paths are qualified dotted Fraktal identities (§4.8). A request routed
 through this root may target the root itself or one descendant, never a peer.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Path</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>prefix</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_PartReceived</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.16.3 EVENT_PART_RECEIVED — confirm identity at station entry via the carrier.
 FALSE with a CARRIER_READ_FAILED fault on a failed read (never silent), FALSE
 silently when no carrier is configured (§3.9 feature selectability).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>RegisterAvailableModel</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8 optional HMI/MES selection catalog. Recipe providers remain pluggable;
 the application registers only the model identities it deliberately exposes.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Id</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ModelId</Type><BitSize>7856</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>CountNok</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Sections 8.11.2 and 11.6: one authoritative NOK outcome path.
 Part.Uid is empty when the optional traceability carrier is not configured.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Reason</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Reason</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_CaptureInto</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The capability walk as one set in Store. The live documents capture into
 _loadSnapshot, so writing them never invalidates an export of _snapshot.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Store</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_ConfigStore</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>SetName</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Kind</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ConfigKind</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ModelIndex</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>info</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigSetInfo</Type><BitSize>2016</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>records</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_ValidateDecision</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ A finite timeout requires a real safe default. An indefinite request may omit
 Default, but every published request still needs at least one selectable option.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Req</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_DecisionRequest</Type><BitSize>7264</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>hasOption</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_NokCyclic</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.16.5 - a trip is never lost and never outlives its alarm. Raised again while
 the alarm table had no room (fail closed: no alarm means no refused Start), and
 re-armed - series and window cleared - once the operator's reset has closed it.]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>_M_PartProcessed</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.16.3 EVENT_PART_PROCESSED — stamp the verdict, write the carrier FIRST
 (result-before-event contract), then raise the event. The Uid and result stay
 published until the next part so the HMI shows the last outcome.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Verdict</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Verdict</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Reason</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Reason</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_LivePassFailed</Name></Method><Method><Name>M_SequenceAwait</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Idx</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Label</Name><Type>STRING(120)</Type><BitSize>968</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Ok</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_SequenceStopNow</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.4/§8.11 — accept a pending Stop BETWEEN cycles: the open profile fragment
 (just the wait step) is abandoned, not published as a production cycle.]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>_M_RouteForceChannel</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Application override resolves ChannelPath in THIS root's approved I/O catalog,
 refuses input/safety/unmapped channels, applies its channel-specific §7.6 permit,
 and routes only an approved mapped output. ForceChannel already owns MANUAL,
 stopped/READY, access and audit. Base fails closed.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>ChannelPath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Force</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>BoolText</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>AnalogText</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_SequenceCountGood</Name></Method><Method><Name>_M_HandleHmiRequest</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.10/§14 — consume one committed OPC UA request exactly once.]]></Comment><Local><Name>modelId</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ModelId</Type><BitSize>7856</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>modeReq</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Mode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>styleReq</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_RunStyle</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>gateReq</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_GatedAction</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>levelReq</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_AccessLevel</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>alarmSlot</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>policyValueValid</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>configKindReq</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ConfigKind</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>__getStopPending</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.4 — TRUE while a stop is requested but the sequence is still finishing
 (running -> stopping). HMI blinks the stop button on this.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>StopPending</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>M_SequencePartStarted</Name></Method><Method><Name>_M_OeeCompute</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §8.5.1 — pure recompute of A/P/Q/OEE from the accumulators (testable in isolation).
 Invalid factors are OMITTED from the product, never assumed 100% (O7).]]></Comment><Local><Name>total</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>denomA</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_PublishStatus</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §6.9/§3.10(a') — overlay the pending stall after the common mirror refresh.]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>M_SetHostEventSink</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §11.6.2 inject an optional OPC UA/MES/REST/MQTT delivery adapter.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Sink</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_HostEventSink</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_EndOfCycle</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ call at the finish step (§8.11.1): publishes the profile; FALSE = stop granted]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>SetModel</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.1b/§3.8 — transactional model change: prepare the whole subtree, then commit.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Id</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ModelId</Type><BitSize>7856</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>SetPersistMedium</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b - keep this root's live configuration on the project's medium too: the
 station data, the line data this root owns, and every model's data, one
 document each ('<root>.station', '<root>.line', '<root>.model<n>'). At start
 the documents are read back and replayed through the owning handlers, staged
 and all-or-nothing per document, before any configuration write is accepted;
 after every accepted write they are written again. A missing document is a
 first start. One the medium confirmed and then lost, or one that no longer
 fits this build, is announced as a lost image under its key (§3.8b restore).
 The native PERSISTENT data stays: it seeds the first documents and is what a
 lost one falls back to. The same medium may serve the set store and the
 access provider. Refused once the restore has started.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Medium</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_PersistMedium</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_PublishToolChanged</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §11.6.1 internal composition seam; not a remote command surface.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Tool</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Value</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_RecoverState</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §8.3(b)/§6.1 — the control-state half of a reset. Closing the alarm alone left the
 machine locked: the Unit's run command and the child commands its mode chain had
 issued both stayed asserted, and §6.1's Execute-drop reset — the only exit from a
 latched terminal state — needs them LOW. A frozen chain cannot drop them itself,
 because a Unit that is not BUSY never calls _M_Dispatch again, so the step holding
 `child.Execute := TRUE` never runs. Nothing else in the system clears it, and the
 next Start re-issues the same already-TRUE input: no rising edge, the child stays
 in ERROR, and the Unit re-adopts the fault through the §8.2 rollup. That is the
 press hard-lock. Returns TRUE when there was something to recover.
 Deliberately does NOT clear ERROR here: Cyclic keeps that ownership (§6.1), so a
 cause that is still live re-faults on the next command edge instead of vanishing.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>M_SequenceAskDecision</Name><Parameter><Name>Req</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_DecisionRequest</Type><BitSize>7264</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_ForcePermitted</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §10.5.1 rules 1 and 3 — may a held force set-point be applied to this
 Unit's outputs right now? The project hardware driver passes the result to
 FB_IoTopologyPublisher.M_ApplyForces every scan, and ForceChannel gates the
 operator request on the identical predicate, so "accepted" and "applied" can
 never disagree. Everything else about a force (access, ownership, direction,
 mapping) is proved elsewhere; this is only the build gate and the mode/state.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>__getModeActive</Name><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Mode</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>ModeActive</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Mode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>_M_RecordSequenceStep</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.13 — keep the published flow chart in step with the chain.
 Called only from _M_SetStep, so every step of every chain lands here exactly
 once per visit and a chain author writes nothing (§1.1 O1). Rows are matched by
 StepNo, appended on first sight and bounded: an overflowing chain publishes the
 first MAX_SEQUENCE_STEPS rows rather than dropping the chart.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>StepNo</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>StepName</Name><Type>STRING(120)</Type><BitSize>968</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Awaits</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_Module</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>AwaitingLabel</Name><Type>STRING(120)</Type><BitSize>968</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>TimeClass</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_TimeClass</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ExpectedTime</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Branch</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §6.12 concurrent leg, 0 = the chain's main line]]></Comment><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>hit</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>path</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_SequenceWarn</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §6.9(e) — a step said something worth recording that is not a failure.
 Deliberately does NOT touch _exec: no fault is adopted, _M_Dispatch keeps
 running, and the chain follows its own recovery path. The ring entry is
 AUTO_RESET come+gone (§8.3(c)) so it can never block the next Start.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Diag</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</Type><BitSize>5568</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>d</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</Type><BitSize>5568</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>slot</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>ListConfigSets</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b — refresh the published listing of stored sets. Read-only, so it is
 gated on CONFIG_SET without the audited write path: seeing which sets exist
 is not replacing a machine's parametrization.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>total</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_SequencePartRecord</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>RecordName</Name><Type>STRING(64)</Type><BitSize>520</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Value</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Minimum</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Maximum</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Target</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>EngUnit</Name><Type>STRING(16)</Type><BitSize>136</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_AskDecision</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §6.11 — publish a typed decision request (single active slot)]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Req</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_DecisionRequest</Type><BitSize>7264</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>candidate</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_DecisionRequest</Type><BitSize>7264</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_PartRecord</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.16.1 — append one measured value to this part's result (test cells).
 FALSE when the bounded record table is full (RESULT_RECORD_REJECTED semantics).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>RecordName</Name><Type>STRING(64)</Type><BitSize>520</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Value</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Minimum</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Maximum</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Target</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>EngUnit</Name><Type>STRING(16)</Type><BitSize>136</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>SetConfigPersistWindow</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b — declare how long an accepted write may take to become durable. The
 clause says "within a declared bounded window", and the point of DECLARING it
 is that different stores have honestly different latencies: a retentive write
 is milliseconds, an MES round trip is not. A deployment that leaves this alone
 gets PL_Fraktal.CONFIG_PERSIST_WINDOW_MS.

 Zero means "durable immediately or not at all", which is the correct
 declaration for a store that either completes in the same scan or has failed.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>WindowMs</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>ReleaseReportAction</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §7.8 — full rollup for the simpler gated Unit actions (Stop, ALARM_RESET,
 CHANGEOVER, MODE_CHANGE, step). Same predicate the gates use. Start has its own
 richer ReleaseReportStart (interlocks); manual has ReleaseReportManual (target).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Gate</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_GatedAction</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Report</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">ST_ReleaseReport</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>CountGood</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §8.11 — called by the chain/verdict glue at part completion]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>SetConfigStore</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b — inject this deployment's parameter-set store at Setup, the same shape
 as SetPartCarrier and the §3.8 recipe provider. Absent means save/load/list are
 not offered at all, published as StorePresent = FALSE — a stated fact rather
 than a request that fails the first time an operator tries it.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Store</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_ConfigStore</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_SequenceRaise</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §6.9 — a step raised a first-out itself. Stamp the flow-chart row with the
 error and its link before adopting the diagnostic, so the §3.13 chart can mark
 the step red and drill into the module that actually failed even when the step
 passed Awaits := 0. Adopting the diagnostic stops the chain: _M_FaultDiag puts
 the Unit in ERROR and _M_Dispatch no longer runs.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Diag</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</Type><BitSize>5568</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>LinkPath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_ConfigPersistCyclic</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b — drive the durability provider and hold the declared window to
 account. "Within a declared bounded window" is a promise, and a promise
 nobody measures is the hope the clause replaces: the window is checked here
 every scan, and exceeding it publishes PersistFailed.]]></Comment><Local><Name>busy</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>elapsed</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_AppendModelConfig</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8a - the manifest walk (M_AppendConfig) with the model-data values of
 AvailableModels[ModelIndex] (0 = the active model). FALSE = no such model.
 For another model the walk yields that model's data only: the rest of the
 manifest is the running station's and is served by index 0.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Pager</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">FB_ConfigPager</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ModelIndex</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>OnOperatorReset</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.14 hook — an accepted operator reset is recovering this Unit. Override to
 withdraw application outputs and reset application-owned mode chains before the
 base releases the run command; call SUPER^.OnOperatorReset() first (§3.14.2).
 Called only when something was actually latched (ERROR or a blocking alarm), so an
 override may assume it is a recovery, not a routine poll.]]></Comment><ReturnType>DINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>_M_NokClearCounts</Name><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>SetSignalTowerConfig</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Startup station-convention seam. Runtime config writes require a registered
 typed capability; this method is not published by OPC UA.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>ParCfg</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_SignalTowerParCfg</Type><BitSize>96</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_DrainRestoreLoss</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b — "restore is fail-closed and never silent". Every module that ran
 M_RestoreStationCfg and found an unrecognized image is holding one report;
 this takes them and annunciates each with the OWNING module's canonical path,
 which is what makes the message actionable instead of "something was lost".

 The event is AUTO_RESET and therefore never blocking: the consequence belongs
 to E_ConfigRestorePolicy, evaluated in ReleaseReportStart, so a station that
 declared DEFAULTS_AND_ANNUNCIATE really does run while the annunciation
 stands. It stays open until an ENGINEER acknowledges it, because nothing
 makes a lost image come back and an event that closed itself would be a lie.]]></Comment><Local><Name>guard</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>path</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>expected</Name><Type>UINT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>found</Name><Type>UINT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_LiveReadFailed</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b - a live document could not be read at start. Announced once (AUTO_RESET,
 gone when the restore completes, through _M_MarkPersistPending); Start meanwhile
 names the restore and configuration writes are refused.]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>_M_StallWalk</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §6.9 — build the pending stall reason: step -> awaited command -> first FALSE condition]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>_M_AnnounceRestoreLoss</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b - publish one lost image and open (or extend) its annunciation.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Path</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Text</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_ApplyConfigWrite</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8e - the subtree first; a line key it does not own goes to the line.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Scope</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>WriteKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Revision</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>TextValue</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RootReady</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_ApplyCapture</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8e - the capture walk is the write walk, line leg included.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Scope</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>WriteKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Revision</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RootReady</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_SaveModelData</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Write the record a model-scoped value was just stored into back to the
 provider: the viewed model's buffer, or the live record for the active model.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>store</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_RecipeStore</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_TakeDecision</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §6.11 — returns the chosen option once and clears the request (0 = none yet)]]></Comment><ReturnType>INT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>16</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>OnAbortInError</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.14 - error-state abort abandons the chain the same way (§6.8).]]></Comment><ReturnType>DINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>_M_OwnsModelRecord</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Record</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigRecord</Type><BitSize>2720</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_LiveKey</Name><ReturnType>STRING(80)</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>648</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Item</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>SetIdealCycle</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §8.5.1 — configure the ideal cycle time (per model, §3.8). 0 disables Performance.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Ms</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_ClearPending</Name></Method><Method><Name>_M_AuditHmiAccepted</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §14.3 security audit for accepted remote mutations. Operational methods may
 additionally emit their domain event (manual action, OEE reset, shelving); this
 record supplies the remote request kind and authenticated user without secrets.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Kind</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_HmiRequestKind</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>TargetPath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Accepted</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>auditable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>auditSlot</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>textValue</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>sourcePath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>__getModelCode</Name><ReturnType>STRING(64)</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>520</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>ModelCode</Name><Type>STRING(64)</Type><BitSize>520</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>_M_OeeUpdate</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §8.5.1 — attribute elapsed time to run/down/idle, recompute factors, sample ring.]]></Comment><Local><Name>currentTime</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>deltaMs</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_LiveApply</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Replay a restored document frozen in _loadSnapshot through the same staged,
 all-or-nothing path a set load takes. A model document goes into that model's
 record (the live one for the active model) and back to the provider; a model
 created at run time whose catalog record did not survive is created again
 from the live record first, then given its values.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Info</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigSetInfo</Type><BitSize>2016</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>index</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_CaptureConfig</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Reuse the capability walk for immutable export and complete-set validation.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>SetName</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Kind</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ConfigKind</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ModelIndex</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_SequenceTakeDecision</Name><ReturnType>INT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>16</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>SetSystemHealth</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ TC3/platform adapter injection. Raw probe values remain OPC-UA-hidden; the
 health publisher validates and republishes the bounded status surface.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Input</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_SystemHealthInput</Type><BitSize>1024</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ParCfg</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_SystemHealthParCfg</Type><BitSize>512</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_Await</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §6.9(b) — named plain-condition wait; returns the condition so steps read naturally]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Idx</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Label</Name><Type>STRING(120)</Type><BitSize>968</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Ok</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_Supports</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.4 — override to declare the type's mode set (baseline: AUTO + MANUAL)]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Mode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Mode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_DeclareDataClass</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8d - declare a project data class on this root, at Setup. The levels are
 defaults: a class the deployment already edited keeps its persisted levels.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>ClassId</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>LabelKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ReadLevel</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_AccessLevel</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>WriteLevel</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_AccessLevel</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>LoadConfigSet</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b — apply a named set. STAGED and ALL-OR-NOTHING.

 Pass 1 validates every record through its owning module's typed handler and
 changes nothing. Only if all of them pass does pass 2 apply them. A
 half-applied machine parametrization is never a valid outcome, and the only
 way to guarantee that is to know the answer for every record before touching
 the first one.

 A record whose capability no longer exists fails pass 1 like any other and is
 REPORTED by name - never silently dropped, because a set that quietly skipped
 the one value that mattered restores a machine to almost its commissioned
 state, which is the failure that is hardest to notice.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>SetName</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>info</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigSetInfo</Type><BitSize>2016</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>OperatorReset</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §8.3(b) — deliberate operator reset of blocking events (release-gated per §7.6/§14).
 ONE operator action has to make the Unit restartable, so this closes the blocking
 events AND clears the latched control state they were reporting: see _M_RecoverState.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>_M_ExportSnapshotLine</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>SetName</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Line</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Token</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>info</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigSetInfo</Type><BitSize>2016</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>record</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigRecord</Type><BitSize>2720</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>SetConfigRestorePolicy</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b — declare what this station DOES about a lost configuration image.
 DEFAULTS_AND_ANNUNCIATE is the shipped default; a station whose commissioned
 values are the difference between a good part and a wrecked tool declares
 BLOCK_UNTIL_ACKNOWLEDGED instead. It is a DEPLOYMENT decision on purpose: no
 module type is in a position to know which of the two its station is, which is
 why a module reporting a loss never decides the consequence of one.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Policy</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ConfigRestorePolicy</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_SupportsRunStyle</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.4.2 — a concrete Unit overrides to opt a mode into SINGLE_STEP/HOLD_TO_RUN.
 Base: only CONTINUOUS.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Style</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_RunStyle</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_NokRaise</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.16.5 - the trip alarm. Severity and category come from the §8.9
 rationalization of NOK_LIMIT_REACHED; the values here are only its proposal.]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>ShelveAlarm</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §8.10 — gated HMI entry: shelve an active alarm's ANNUNCIATION (control untouched).
 §7.7 ALARM_SHELVE + audit; refuses SAFETY / unrationalized reasons (AlarmLog rules).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Slot</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>DurationS</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>ExportCurrentConfig</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>SetName</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Kind</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ConfigKind</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ModelIndex</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Token</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>info</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigSetInfo</Type><BitSize>2016</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>record</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigRecord</Type><BitSize>2720</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>Stop</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.3 — stop after the current cycle]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>ExportConfigSetLine</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b — serve one line of a set's JSON document. Line 0 is the header and
 1..RecordCount are the records, so a client pulls a movable document a line
 at a time and no full document buffer ever exists in the PLC - the same
 paging discipline QUERY_CONFIG already uses for the manifest.

 This is what makes a set MOVABLE, which is the point of naming sets at all: a
 station's commissioning can leave the controller as text, be reviewed,
 diffed, version-controlled and put on the next machine.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>SetName</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Line</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>info</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigSetInfo</Type><BitSize>2016</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>record</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigRecord</Type><BitSize>2720</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_ChartRevCyclic</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.13/§3.10.2 — raise the manifest revision ONCE the flow chart has stopped
 growing, rather than once per row discovered.

 The rows are the manifest's largest and most volatile contributor and they
 appear one at a time as the chain visits them, so a per-row bump turned one
 mode entry into one full-manifest refetch per step. This waits for the burst
 to settle and then charges for it once.

 The delay is bounded and small (PL_Fraktal.CHART_REV_SETTLE_MS): the chart
 appears fractionally later and COMPLETE, instead of promptly and then being
 refetched fourteen more times.]]></Comment><Local><Name>elapsed</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>OnInit</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.14 hook — one-shot after first operational scan]]></Comment><ReturnType>DINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>UnshelveAlarm</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §8.10 — gated HMI entry: restore annunciation.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Slot</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>CaptureConfig</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8c - the root authority for a capture. Deliberately the same gate, the same
 ownership check and the same ConfigRev bump as WriteConfig: a capture is a
 write whose value came from the machine, and it is no more and no less
 privileged than one the operator typed (§3.8c(d)).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>TargetPath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>WriteKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Revision</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>CreateModel</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Append an inactive provider record. Live recipe and existing ordinals stay fixed.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>ModelCode</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>SourceIndex</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>FromSet</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>SetName</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>info</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigSetInfo</Type><BitSize>2016</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>record</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigRecord</Type><BitSize>2720</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>source</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_ConfigStore</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>sourceName</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_SetStep</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §6.5 — the ONE line per step: record for the §6.9 walk AND the §8.11.4 profiler]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>StepNo</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>StepName</Name><Type>STRING(120)</Type><BitSize>968</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Awaits</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_Module</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>AwaitingLabel</Name><Type>STRING(120)</Type><BitSize>968</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>TimeClass</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_TimeClass</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ExpectedTime</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>e</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_CondRecord</Type><BitSize>976</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>SubmitDecision</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §6.11 authoritative decision entry. START_STOP is the access gate because the
 answer advances a running Unit chain; option-specific process releases append
 through _M_AppendDecisionInterlocks. A stale/invalid answer never latches.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Option</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Report</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">ST_ReleaseReport</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>SetNokPolicy</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §3.16.5 - the Unit's NOK-part limit, given by the composition root (editing
 it on site waits for a station that asks). Refused - policy unchanged - unless it
 is the layout this Unit was compiled against and each rule is off or well formed:
 InSeries >= 0, and the window either off (WindowCount = WindowNok = 0) or
 1 <= WindowNok <= WindowCount <= NOK_WINDOW_MAX. An accepted policy counts
 afresh; a trip already raised stays until the operator resets it.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Cfg</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_NokPolicyParCfg</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>compiled</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_NokPolicyParCfg</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_WriteBaseConfig</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Framework-owned typed handlers. Stable keys are independent of browse paths;
 capability revision 1 accepts exact enum ordinals and only while READY.

 Commit := FALSE validates and stores nothing — the staging pass of a §3.8b set
 load. The root's own ModePolicy keys are published as STATION_CFG
 capabilities, so they are in every station set and have to stage through the
 same validator that writes them, for the same reason every module's do.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>TargetPath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>WriteKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Revision</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>TextValue</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Commit</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>key</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>shield</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ModeSwitchShield</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>style</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ModeSwitchStyle</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_AppendConfig</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.10.2 — Unit facets after the composite walk (own catalog + children):
 model catalog and per-mode switch policy, both static between config edits.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Pager</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">FB_ConfigPager</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>metaIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>item</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>writeKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>labelKey</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ std.config.modePolicy.<mode ordinal>.<shield|style>]]></Comment><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>meta</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_AlarmMeta</Type><BitSize>4224</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>seqIdx</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>seqBase</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_ClearDecisionState</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Clear the complete public slot and all private latches atomically.]]></Comment><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>OnModeChanged</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.14 hook — after the new mode is committed]]></Comment><ReturnType>DINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>NewMode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Mode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>OldMode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Mode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>OnCommandStart</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §11.6: CHANGEOVER starts when its guided sequence actually starts, not
 merely when the operator selects the mode or transactionally loads a model.]]></Comment><ReturnType>DINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>SetHoldRun</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.4.2 — HMI HOLD_TO_RUN input. NON-SAFETY (§9): never a dead-man; interlocks
 still apply at every step. TRUE only while the operator holds the button.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Held</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>ForceChannel</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §10.5.1 centralized force authority. Only an idle MANUAL Unit may reach the
 application resolver; that resolver still proves root ownership, OUTPUT,
 non-safety identity, mapping and the channel-specific release.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>ChannelPath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Force</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>BoolText</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>AnalogText</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_SequenceEndOfCycle</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>_M_ResumeSequencesAfterError</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §6.9 — the ERROR state ended: clear the flow-chart error marks and re-arm
 every attached chain so the step that raised the fault re-evaluates its
 command. A project writes nothing for this (§1.1 O1).]]></Comment><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_AppendManualInterlocks</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §7.8 — target-aware hook for the MANUAL release rollup: a concrete Unit
 overrides to append the §7.6 Release<Function> conditions of the SPECIFIC target
 module. Base delegates to the Unit-level hook (non-breaking default).]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>TargetPath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Value</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Report</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">ST_ReleaseReport</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>Start</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.3/§6 intro — the run IS a §6.1 command.
 §7.8: ReleaseReportStart is the authoritative machine gate as well as the
 operator explanation, so a concrete Unit cannot report an interlock it ignores.
 Build directly into the published response storage: ST_ReleaseReport is too
 large for nested by-value/local copies on a small TwinCAT task stack.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>M_SequencePartProcessed</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Verdict</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Verdict</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Reason</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Reason</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_RestartSequences</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §6.8 - restart every attached chain. The base calls it where a chain can never
 resume (first scan, mode change, abort, abort in error). Whether a fresh run
 command or an operator reset RESTARTS the chain or lets it resume where an
 error stopped it is the project's policy (§6.9(d)), so a project that wants a
 restart there calls this one line from OnCommandStart / OnOperatorReset.]]></Comment><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>SetDataClassLevel</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8d/§7.7(b) - edit a class's read or write level. The same gate as
 every other policy edit (ACCESS_POLICY), audited through the mailbox.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>ClassId</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Level</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ForWrite</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>levelReq</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_AccessLevel</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>ManualHeldTo</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §7.6.1a — single gated entry for a HELD manual action (hold-to-run). Same
 gates as ManualCommandTo: this Unit in MANUAL (§3.4) and MANUAL access
 (§7.7). Held := TRUE latches the request; FALSE releases it immediately.

 The release is explicit AND the latch expires, deliberately both: an explicit
 release stops the motion the moment the operator lets go, and the deadline
 stops it when no release ever arrives because the client vanished. Relying on
 either alone leaves one of those two cases moving.

 Hold-to-run over a transport is NON-SAFETY (no dead-man, TC3 §7.6): the
 enabling device is the safety-rated fact, derived below from the §9 facet and
 carried to the module, which weighs it itself.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>TargetPath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Value</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Held</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>auditSlot</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>ReleaseReportManual</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §7.8 — full rollup of why a manual command to Target would be refused (§7.6.1).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>TargetPath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Value</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Report</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">ST_ReleaseReport</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_EngineeringCyclic</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §7.5.2 — the standing annunciation: one LOW/SYSTEM/AUTO_RESET event per
 registered gate, for as long as that gate is registered.

 Why each choice is the way it is, because every one of them is load-bearing:
   AUTO_RESET  a MANUAL_RESET event refuses Start (§8.3(b)), which would make
               commissioning gates block the commissioning they exist to serve;
   LOW/SYSTEM  the lowest priority and the lowest risk class - this says how the
               software was BUILT, not that the process or safety is impaired,
               and a louder class would displace real alarms (§8.9);
   unclearable OperatorReset only closes MANUAL_RESET events, so no operator
               action reaches this one, and its §8.9 record is not shelvable, so
               §8.10 cannot silence it either. It closes when the gate is gone -
               which, gates being build constants, means a new download.]]></Comment><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>gateCount</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_SequenceAnnotate</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §6.9 — attach an error or a message to a flow-chart row.

 One slot per (row, kind): re-annotating the same row with the same kind
 overwrites rather than accumulating, which is what makes it safe for the
 per-visit message latch to call this without tracking slots.

 Returns FALSE when the table is full. The CALLER has already set the row flag
 by then, deliberately: a full table costs the text, never the mark, so the
 chart still shows that something happened here (§5.6 degrade, never mislead).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>RowIdx</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>IsError</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Key</Name><Type>STRING(120)</Type><BitSize>968</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>SourcePath</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>slot</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_InitModePolicy</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.4.1/§3.14.4 — default per-mode switch policy. Station config (§3.8a) may
 overwrite ModePolicy[] after this. By FRAMEWORK DEFAULT a mode change while a
 sequence runs performs an IMMEDIATE software abort (E-stop-like, not a safety
 function, §3.14.4) — so Style defaults to IMMEDIATE. GRACEFUL completion is an
 opt-in: a Unit overrides OnModeExit to stop-after-cycle, or station config sets
 Style := GRACEFUL for a mode. Shield only governs acceptance while running.]]></Comment><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_PublishMaterialChanged</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §11.6.1 internal composition seam; not a remote command surface.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Material</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Value</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_ConfigAccessOf</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8e/§3.8d - the access walk is the write walk, line leg included, so a line
 value is checked against the level the line declared for it.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Scope</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>WriteKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Grant</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">ST_ConfigAccess</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_IsLineKey</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8e - TRUE when a (Scope, WriteKey) the subtree did not own names a value of
 the line this Unit references: the line is published under this Unit's own
 scope, and its keys alone begin 'line.'.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Scope</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>WriteKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>RequestLocalReset</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Application-only seam for an ordinary hardwired fault-reset/acknowledge button,
 mirroring RequestLocalControl (§9.8): it is a METHOD, not OPC UA data, so remote
 clients still go through the access-gated OPERATOR_RESET request and cannot reach
 this path. A cabinet button IS its own authorization (physical presence), so it
 carries no §7.7 session check — but the reset is still audited as a §8.3 event,
 and it recovers exactly the same state as an operator reset, never more.
 The composition root calls this from its hardware driver on the button's rising
 edge, once per root Unit it should clear.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>auditSlot</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_RouteManual</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §7.6.1 — route a manual command to the module that owns TargetPath, through
 the SAME registered-child walk that already carries configuration writes.

 This used to return FALSE and leave every Unit to hand-write its own routing
 chain. That is a call a project must remember for correctness (§1.1 O1), and
 it failed exactly as O1 predicts: the press registered eight children and
 routed three, so five modules published manual commands the HMI rendered and
 the Unit silently refused. A registered child is now commandable BECAUSE it
 is registered.

 An override still wins, so a Unit with genuinely special routing keeps it;
 it should call SUPER^ first and keep its own answer only when the base
 declines.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>TargetPath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Value</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_SequenceStopPending</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.4 — a chain polls this at its between-cycles wait step.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>_M_AppendDecisionInterlocks</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §6.11 option-aware release seam. The base validates session, active prompt and
 option identity; a concrete Unit appends the ordinary process conditions that a
 "continue"-style option must satisfy. Safety and child interlocks still remain
 authoritative at their owning modules.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Option</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Report</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">ST_ReleaseReport</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_LiveModelsKept</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Model data is kept per model when this root registered its own record
 (M_RegisterModelData) with a provider that stores records, and every PAR_CFG
 value of the walk lives in that record. A child's model data belongs to the
 child's recipe, which this root cannot select per model.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>store</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_RecipeStore</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>info</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigSetInfo</Type><BitSize>2016</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>record</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigRecord</Type><BitSize>2720</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_ShiftTick</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Evaluate only at a finite boundary, or after an empty-calendar edit.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Now</Name><Type>DATE_AND_TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Synchronized</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>idx</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>started</Name><Type>DATE_AND_TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>ending</Name><Type>DATE_AND_TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>target</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>crossed</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>quality</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_ConfigSetHalfApplied</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b — a record passed staging and then failed to apply. This cannot
 happen: both run the same validator on the same data in the same scan. If it
 ever does, the machine is half-parametrized and that is a state the standard
 says is never valid - so it is escalated as a BLOCKING alarm rather than
 returned as a FALSE somebody might retry. A framework defect that leaves a
 machine half-configured has to stop it, not inconvenience it.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Scope</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Key</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_RegisterModelData</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §3.8a - declare this root's own recipe record (its ParCfg) and the
 provider it is loaded from. The PAR_CFG values registered inside it become
 editable for EVERY model the root offers (AvailableModels), not only the
 active one, and an edit is written back to the provider's record so a
 changeover keeps it - when the provider is also an I_RecipeStore.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>pData</Name><Type GUID="{18071995-0000-0000-0000-000000000018}">PVOID</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Size</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RecipeKey</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Provider</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_RecipeProvider</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>OnAbort</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.14 - an aborted mode chain is abandoned, never resumed: restart every
 attached chain so the next command starts at N000 (§6.8).]]></Comment><ReturnType>DINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>_M_BeginSequenceScan</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §6.10 — reset every attached chain's shared transition result once per
 PLC cycle, before _M_Dispatch drives any step action. This is why a project
 never calls M_BeginScan itself, and why an SFC/LD/FBD chart needs no wiring
 to be safe against a stale ADVANCE (O1).]]></Comment><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_RouteConfigWrite</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b — route a published editable field to the module that registered it.
 WriteConfig already owns access and root-path checks; the recursive walk finds
 the owner by Scope, and that module rechecks revision, type, range, domain and
 its own invariants before storing. A type whose values are declared through
 M_RegisterConfig* therefore needs no override at all, which is the point: a new
 module type costs no routing code (§1.1 O1). Framework-owned keys never reach
 here — _M_WriteBaseConfig answers those first. An override that adds
 hand-written routing shall call SUPER^ first and keep its own answer only when
 the base declines.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>TargetPath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>WriteKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Revision</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>TextValue</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_DecisionMatches</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Full value comparison makes repeated presentation idempotent while treating a
 changed option/default/timeout as a different request that must not overwrite.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Req</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_DecisionRequest</Type><BitSize>7264</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_CloseShift</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §8.5.2(b) - one operation in one scan: record the ending shift as its figures stood,
 then reset the per-shift counts and OEE accumulators (the trend ring is kept). A
 boundary on an unsynchronized clock still closes - stopping the accounting would
 lose more than a late boundary does - and the record says so.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Now</Name><Type>DATE_AND_TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Synchronized</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>auditSlot</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_SyncModelCatalog</Name><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>j</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>id</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ModelId</Type><BitSize>7856</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>exists</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>found</Name><Type>UINT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>info</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigSetInfo</Type><BitSize>2016</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>record</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigRecord</Type><BitSize>2720</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>SetSessionTimeout</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §7.7 persistent idle timeout (0 = never), self-gated by ACCESS_POLICY.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>TimeoutMs</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>SetRunStyle</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.4.2 — HMI selects the run style for the active mode. Modes that don't opt in
 (see _M_SupportsRunStyle) reject non-CONTINUOUS. Access: MODE_CHANGE-gated (§7.7).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Style</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_RunStyle</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_ProbeUnit</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ minimal Unit for the base suite: 2-step looping chain, one wait-classed step]]></Comment><BitSize>2776768</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_UnitBase</ExtendsType><SubItem><Name>SimA</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>2776512</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SimB</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>2776520</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SimFault</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ deterministic fault injection for base-path tests]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>2776528</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ModeChangedCount</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>2776544</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ModeExitCount</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>2776576</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ModeExitFirstCount</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>2776608</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>LastNewMode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Mode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>2776640</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>LastOldMode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Mode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>2776672</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>LastRequestedMode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Mode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>2776704</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><Method><Name>OnModeChanged</Name><ReturnType>DINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>NewMode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Mode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>OldMode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Mode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_TestClearDecision</Name></Method><Method><Name>Setup</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Name</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_TestTakeDecision</Name><ReturnType>INT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>16</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>_M_Dispatch</Name></Method><Method><Name>M_TestAskDecision</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Test-probe seam for the protected §6.11 host service.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Req</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_DecisionRequest</Type><BitSize>7264</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>OnModeExit</Name><ReturnType>DINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>FirstCall</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RequestedMode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Mode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_Unit_Tests</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ FB_UnitBase suite: mode rejection, run-as-command, stall key, wait-class
 derived Starved, cycle publication, mode change = immediate software abort by default.]]></Comment><BitSize>39326784</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="TcUnit">FB_TestSuite</ExtendsType><SubItem><Name>_u</Name><Type>FB_ProbeUnit</Type><BitSize>2776768</BitSize><BitOffs>33574912</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_uCfg</Name><Type>FB_ProbeUnit</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ The config-capability test needs a Unit that is READY. _u is not: the
 stall test starts it and FB_ProbeUnit only reaches its _M_EndOfCycle stop
 point when SimB is set, so a Stop() is never granted and it stays BUSY.
 A shared fixture in a non-shareable state is what that test was really
 measuring; give it its own.]]></Comment><BitSize>2776768</BitSize><BitOffs>36351680</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_w</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>39128448</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_wCfg</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>39128456</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_pager</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_ConfigPager</Type><BitSize>512</BitSize><BitOffs>39128512</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_page</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigPage</Type><BitSize>197760</BitSize><BitOffs>39129024</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>Unit_run_stall_classes_and_cycle</Name></Method><Method><Name>Sequence_rows_belong_to_the_active_mode</Name></Method><Method><Name>Unit_mode_change_is_estop_by_default</Name></Method><Method><Name>Unit_config_capability_is_typed_and_fail_closed</Name><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>found</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>pageIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>pageCount</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_DeviceConnector</Name><BitSize>64</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_Module</ExtendsType><Method><Name>__getLastSeen</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ timestamp of last healthy heartbeat (Core §2.7)]]></Comment><ReturnType>DATE_AND_TIME</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getLinked</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ session up AND heartbeat healthy (Core §3.15.2)]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getLinkReason</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ first-out link/protocol reason when not Linked]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>5568</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>Connect</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>Disconnect</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceId</Name><Value>2373</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_HbResult</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ FB_DeviceConnectorBase transport contract (Core §3.15)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BaseType>DINT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>PENDING</Text><Enum>0</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>OK</Text><Enum>1</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>FAIL</Text><Enum>2</Enum></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>qualified_only</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_LinkReaction</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §3.15 — configured reaction of the fronting CM to link loss]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BaseType>DINT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>HOLD</Text><Enum>0</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>ABORT</Text><Enum>1</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>MODE_STOP</Text><Enum>2</Enum></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>qualified_only</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_DeviceConnectorBase</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §3.15 written once: session + heartbeat + LinkTimeout loss confirm +
 bounded exponential backoff reconnect + NO self-resume of dependents (that is
 the fronting CM's contract). A transport implements only _M_Open/_M_Close/
