 the same shape as SetDirectionalPermits: a method (not an OPC UA write), and the
 condition is re-evaluated every scan so a manual command obeys the same rule.

 This replaces a SIM-only force hook that used to drive Cond[1] directly. That
 hook was the ONLY writer of the condition, so the slot an operator sees as
 "area safe" could be moved by a test and by nothing else: a reusable type
 published an interlock its application had no way to supply (§7.2.1), and the
 bypass shipped in every release build (§5.7). Driving the real condition is
 also strictly better test evidence - T3 now exercises the shipped path.

 Defaults TRUE: a station that declares no area interlock is not gated by one.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Ok</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>DescriptionKey</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>AbortRecipe</Name></Method><Method><Name>RestoreOutputs</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Symmetric counterpart to WithdrawOutputs, for an owning sequence that withdrew a
 cylinder to hold a phase and now wants it driving again — a press dwell whose
 two-hand button was released and re-pressed, where the force comes from the valve
 latched by the already-completed EXTEND, so nothing else would re-energize it.
 Re-asserts ONLY the last commanded direction and ONLY while that direction's own
 permit is satisfied, so it can never restore an output the interlock is withholding:
 the caller asks, this module still decides. Idempotent; safe to call every scan.
 Not a certified enable — the safety system remains authoritative (§9).]]></Comment><Local><Name>permitted</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_Dispatch</Name><Local><Name>ext</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>reached</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>coil</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>d</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</Type><BitSize>5568</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>OnCyclic</Name><ReturnType>DINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>AppendDirectionalRelease</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Pure release-query companion to SetDirectionalPermits. The owning Unit uses
