</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>cbWrite</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Count of bytes actually written ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>544</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property><Property><Name>hide_all_locals</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Tc2_System">FB_FileClose</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Closes a file stream. ]]></Comment><BitSize>1408</BitSize><SubItem><Name>sNetId</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_System">T_AmsNetID</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Ams net id ]]></Comment><BitSize>192</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>hFile</Name><Type>UINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ File handle obtained through 'open' ]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>256</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bExecute</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Rising edge starts command execution ]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>272</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tTimeout</Name><Type>TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Maximum time allowed for the execution of this ADS command ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>288</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>5000</DateTime></Default><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bBusy</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Busy flag ]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>320</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bError</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Error flag ]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>328</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nErrId</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ ADS error code ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>352</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property><Property><Name>hide_all_locals</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_FilePersistMedium</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §3.8b - the FILE medium (E_ConfigStore.FILE_JSON) on Tc2_System file
 services. Each key is two files in one folder, '<key>.a' and '<key>.b', and a
 write always replaces the slot NOT holding the newest valid copy, so a write
 cut short by a power loss leaves the previous document whole.

 Every file is an 80-byte text header line, then the document unchanged:
   FRAKTAL-DOC 1 G=<generation> L=<length> K=<key CRC> C=<data CRC> H=<header CRC>
 in hexadecimal, so a set document stays readable in an editor. K binds a file
 to its key (a copy renamed to another key is refused), C checks the document
 and H the header. The highest valid generation wins on read.

 Both headers are read again before every write: the slot to replace and the
 next generation always come from what is on storage NOW, never from an earlier
 conclusion. A slot that cannot be READ (a file-service error other than "not
 found") is not a slot that is empty: a read then answers Ok = FALSE - the
 medium could not answer, nothing is claimed lost - and a write is refused
 without touching either file. Only content that reads but does not verify is
 treated as damaged.

 The generation each key was last CONFIRMED written at is kept PERSISTENT
 (it is not secret). A read that finds nothing valid where something was
 confirmed, or finds an older generation, reports Lost. TwinCAT stores the
 table at shutdown or on an explicit persistent write, so it can lag and never
 vouches for a write that did not happen; a stale marker can only miss a loss.
 The table is keyed by F_Crc32(folder + key), so retargeting the medium never
 claims a loss for files that were simply never written there. Keys beyond
 MAX_PERSIST_KEYS still work, without loss detection.

 Not symbol-readable: documents pass through the caller's buffer, so this
 medium may hold credentials (M_Confidential). On an IPC image with a write
 filter (UWF/EWF/FBWF), the folder must be excluded or every write reverts at
 the next boot. Files are created by the TwinCAT runtime's account; the
 folder's ACL decides who else may change them.]]></Comment><BitSize>26816</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_PersistMediumBase</ExtendsType><SubItem><Name>StorageError</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ last file-service error (0 = none)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>7488</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_confirmedKey</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>48</Elements></ArrayInfo><BitSize>1536</BitSize><BitOffs>7520</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>TcPersistent</Name></Property><Property><Name>OPC.UA.DA</Name><Value>0</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_confirmedGen</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>48</Elements></ArrayInfo><BitSize>1536</BitSize><BitOffs>9056</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>TcPersistent</Name></Property><Property><Name>OPC.UA.DA</Name><Value>0</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_folder</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize><BitOffs>10592</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_where</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_System">E_OpenPath</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>11888</BitOffs><Default><EnumText>E_OpenPath.PATH_BOOTPATH</EnumText></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_foldersMade</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>11904</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_mkPos</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>11920</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_phase</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ The active request.]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>11936</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_keyCrc</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>11968</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_slot</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>12000</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_hdrValid</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>2</Elements></ArrayInfo><BitSize>1