 -1 when none is left. A drive root ('C:\') and a leading UNC prefix are skipped.]]></Comment><ReturnType>INT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>16</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>StartAt</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>p</Name><Type PointerTo="1">BYTE</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>Setup</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Where the files live. Where = PATH_GENERIC takes an absolute Folder, for
 example 'C:\ProgramData\Fraktal\Station\'; PATH_BOOTPATH is relative to the
 TwinCAT Boot directory ('' = the directory itself). Missing folders are
 created on the first request. At most 160 characters; a trailing separator is
 added. Refused once a request was queued: one medium never splits a document
 over two folders.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Folder</Name><Type>STRING(200)</Type><BitSize>1608</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Where</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_System">E_OpenPath</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>n</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>p</Name><Type PointerTo="1">BYTE</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_Step</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>best</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>confirmed</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>keyPath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_ConfirmedGen</Name><ReturnType>UDINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_Confirm</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Record the generation just written for this key (the persistent marker).]]></Comment><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_ParseHeader</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ A header is valid when re-building it from its own fields gives the same 80
 bytes: that checks the labels, the padding, the header CRC and the key in one
 comparison. Its fields are kept per slot; the payload read rebuilds the
 expected header from them for the slot it is reading.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Slot</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>fileGen</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>fileLen</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>fileKey</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>fileCrc</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_Newest</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The slot with the highest valid header generation, 0 when neither is valid.]]></Comment><ReturnType>INT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>16</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>M_Kind</Name><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ConfigStore</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_LocalAccessProvider</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §7.7(c) — DEFAULT local provider: a durable user table. Remote/central
 auth (server, LDAP via gateway) substitutes behind I_AccessProvider later.

 §14 - a PIN is never stored: each user keeps a random-per-registration salt and
 an iterated SHA-256 of salt and PIN, and the table is hidden from the ADS symbol
 table and OPC UA. Hiding is the control that matters for a short PIN - four
 digits fall to an offline search whatever the hash - so the hash's job is that a
 dump, backup or retained file does not hand the PINs out as text.

 TwinCAT restores PERSISTENT data by symbol and a hidden variable has none, so a
 hidden table cannot be PERSISTENT (IMPLEMENTATION_NOTES §154). The table is kept
 instead as one CRC-protected image document on an I_PersistMedium (§163): by
 default a file medium in the runtime's TwinCAT Boot directory, or the project's
 own medium (M_UseMedium) - which must be confidential, so a retentive-memory
 pool, readable over ADS, is refused. The medium keeps two copies, never
 overwrites the newest, and reports a document it confirmed and then lost. The
 owning root's FB_AccessManager drives restore and save through I_AccessStore
 every scan: a project calls nothing to make its users durable.]]></Comment><BitSize>52480</BitSize><Implements Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_AccessProvider</Implements><Implements Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_AccessStore</Implements><SubItem><Name>Restored</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ the retained table has been read (or there was none)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>192</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Durable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ every registration so far is in a written image]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>200</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>StorageError</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ last medium error (0 = none)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>224</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_instancePath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ '<project>.<path>.<instance>': hashed into the default key, so two providers -
