 because a project attaches several to the same data (the catalog defines
 channel identity, the hardware driver moves live values), and two copies
 of this flag would let them disagree about whether a force is live.]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>9533480</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>OPC.UA.DA</Name><Value>0</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_IoTopologyPublisher</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §10.5.1 infrastructure service. Owns the reusable bounded-table,
 validation, health and diagnostic-join algorithms; project code supplies only
 physical topology metadata and live values. This is not a module tier.]]></Comment><BitSize>192</BitSize><SubItem><Name>_data</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">ST_FieldbusTopology</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>OPC.UA.DA</Name><Value>0</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_attached</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>M_SetForceable</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Explicit commissioning capability. Direction alone never enables forcing;
 the project marks only mapped, non-safety outputs that its Unit resolver owns.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>NodeIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ChannelIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Forceable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_SetForce</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §10.5.1 — arm or clear one held force set-point, addressed by the unique
 channel Path (§4.8) the HMI sent. Called once per operator request, never per
 scan, so the linear search over the bounded table is the right cost here.

 This method is NOT an authority. Access (§7.7 MANUAL), Unit mode/state and the
 §7.5 OUTPUT_FORCING gate are all proved upstream in FB_UnitBase.ForceChannel;
 what is rechecked here is the physical contract that only this table knows:
 the channel exists, it is an OUTPUT, and the project marked it Forceable.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>ChannelPath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>OwnerRootPath</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §4.8 - the qualified identity of the root routing this request. Only a
 channel owned by that root or one of its descendants may be forced, so a
 request routed through one root can never reach a peer station's outputs.]]></Comment><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Force</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>BoolValue</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>AnalogValue</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>n</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>c</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>ownerPrefix</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_SetAllHealth</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Legacy/fallback: force one health verdict on every node. Kept for transports
 or projects that cannot read per-node bus state (e.g. no fieldbus master).
 Prefer M_SetNodeState so the HMI shows each node's REAL state.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Healthy</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>n</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>c</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_SetNodeState</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §10.5.1: publish ONE node's real fieldbus state, independent of any
 control/safety verdict. State is the neutral E_NodeState the HMI renders
 (INIT/PREOP/SAFEOP/OPERATIONAL/FAULT/OFFLINE); LinkOk mirrors the physical
 link. Channel Quality follows link health (a down node's values are stale).
 The caller derives State/LinkOk from the actual bus master (see FB_EcBusHealth
 for EtherCAT); node state is NOT conditioned by Control-On or safety.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>NodeIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>State</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_NodeState</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>LinkOk</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>c</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_SetDigitalValue</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>NodeIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ChannelIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Value</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_SetAnalogValue</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §10.5.1 — publish an analog channel's live value (the analogue of
 M_SetDigitalValue, and live-tier on the HMI for the same reason).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>NodeIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ChannelIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Value</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_Validate</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>n</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>c</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>n2</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>c2</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>Setup</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>DataRef</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">ST_FieldbusTopology</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ResetData</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>n</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>c</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_ApplyForces</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §10.5.1 rule 3 — the per-scan permit for held forces, called by the
 project hardware driver with its owning Unit's FB_UnitBase.M_ForcePermitted().

 The falling edge is what makes the rule real: leaving MANUAL, starting a mode,
 or a build without the §7.5 gate WITHDRAWS every force rather than leaving a
 set-point contending with live application logic. Deriving the edge from the
 published flag itself (not from instance state) keeps every publisher attached
 to this table in agreement about whether a force is live.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Enabled</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>n</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>c</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_DefineAnalogChannel</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §10.5.1 — declare a non-boolean channel: an analog input, or the process-image
 bytes of a communication terminal (an EL6001 status/data byte is a channel of
 the bus like any other, and an operator diagnosing a dead link needs to see it).
 Identical validation to M_DefineDigitalChannel; only Kind and the unit differ.
 The unit has ONE source per channel: a UnitCode (the published Unit text is then
 derived from it), or - only for a unit E_EngUnit lacks - EngUnit text. A channel
 given both is a mapping defect and is refused, never silently resolved.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>NodeIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ChannelIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Tag</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>DescriptionKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Address</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Path</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ModulePath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Dir</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ChannelDir</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>EngUnit</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ '' with a UnitCode, or when the raw count has no unit]]></Comment><Type>STRING(16)</Type><BitSize>136</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>UnitCode</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ E_EngUnit.NONE when the unit is given as EngUnit text]]></Comment><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_EngUnit</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_EffectiveBool</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §10.5.1 — the value the hardware driver should actually write to this
 digital output: the held force set-point while forcing is permitted, otherwise
 the application's own value. It RETURNS the value, so a driver line still reads
 as a plain assignment (the same shape as _M_State on a module):

     GVL_PressIO._101K301A := _publisher.M_EffectiveBool(
         NodeIndex := 4, ChannelIndex := 1, Value := SlideHal.ExtendOut);

 An out-of-range or unforced channel returns Value unchanged, so a mapping
 mistake degrades to ordinary control rather than to a stuck output (§5.6).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>NodeIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ChannelIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Value</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_EffectiveAnalog</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §10.5.1 — the analog twin of M_EffectiveBool, same contract.]]></Comment><ReturnType>REAL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>NodeIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ChannelIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Value</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_ApplyDiagnostic</Name><Parameter><Name>Diagnostic</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</Type><BitSize>5568</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_DefineNode</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Index</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Name</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>DescriptionKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>TypeId</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Address</Name><Type>STRING(40)</Type><BitSize>328</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ParentIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_Reject</Name><Parameter><Name>Text</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_ApplyDiagnosticToTag</Name><Parameter><Name>Diagnostic</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</Type><BitSize>5568</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Tag</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>n</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>c</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_DefineDigitalChannel</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>NodeIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ChannelIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Tag</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>DescriptionKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Address</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Path</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ModulePath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Dir</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ChannelDir</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_BeginDiagnosticRefresh</Name><Local><Name>n</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>c</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_IoTopologyPublisher_Tests</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §10.5.1 reusable topology mechanism: bounded registration, validation,
 live value/health refresh and exact-tag diagnostic correlation.]]></Comment><BitSize>62181696</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="TcUnit">FB_TestSuite</ExtendsType><SubItem><Name>_publisher</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_IoTopologyPublisher</Type><BitSize>192</BitSize><BitOffs>33574912</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_publisherDuplicate</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_IoTopologyPublisher</Type><BitSize>192</BitSize><BitOffs>33575104</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_data</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_FieldbusTopology</Type><BitSize>9533504</BitSize><BitOffs>33575296</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_dataDuplicate</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_FieldbusTopology</Type><BitSize>9533504</BitSize><BitOffs>43108800</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_d</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</Type><BitSize>5568</BitSize><BitOffs>52642304</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_wired</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>52647872</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_duplicateWired</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>52647880</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_unitPublisher</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_IoTopologyPublisher</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Unit rows: one table of their own, because the refused definition marks
 its table invalid. The other two rows read only their own slots.]]></Comment><BitSize>192</BitSize><BitOffs>52647936</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_unitData</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_FieldbusTopology</Type><BitSize>9533504</BitSize><BitOffs>52648128</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_unitsWired</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>62181632</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>UnitCode_derives_the_unit_text</Name></Method><Method><Name>A_code_and_a_text_together_are_refused</Name></Method><Method><Name>No_code_keeps_the_catalog_text</Name></Method><Method><Name>Publishes_value_health_and_diagnostic</Name></Method><Method><Name>Rejects_duplicate_channel_identity</Name></Method><Method><Name>_M_WireUnits</Name></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_DigitalInputParCfg</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §3.8 ParCfg (SchemaVersion first). The composition root assigns it; the
 type has no recipe provider, so this initializer is the layout FB_DigitalInputCM
 checks against. v2 appended DebounceTime; its default reproduces v1.]]></Comment><BitSize>64</BitSize><SubItem><Name>SchemaVersion</Name><Type>UINT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs><Default><Value>2</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>DebounceTime</Name><Type>TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ How long the HAL value must differ from the published Value, continuously,
 before Value follows it. T#0MS passes it through in the same scan. Above
 FB_DigitalInputCM.DI_DEBOUNCE_MAX it is a configuration defect, not a filter.]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#0MS</DateTime></Default></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_DigitalInputHal</Name><BitSize>16</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Value</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Quality</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>8</BitOffs><Default><Bool>true</Bool></Default></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_DigitalInputParCmd</Name><BitSize>8</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Reserved</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ passive monitor: physical four-structure contract, no command payload]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_DigitalInputOutCmd</Name><BitSize>8</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Reserved</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ passive monitor: no command result]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_DigitalInputOutImm</Name><BitSize>664</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Value</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Quality</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>8</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>IoTag</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>16</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_DigitalInputCM</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Basic passive digital-input CM. Owning logic consumes semantic Value; the
 project catalog injects the physical identity separately from the HAL.
 A bouncing contact is settled here, at the signal's owner (§7.2.1), through
 ParCfg.DebounceTime - never by a sequence that happens to read it. Bad quality
 or a configuration the type cannot honour publishes Value FALSE, Quality FALSE
 (§5.6): an input that is silently slow or stale is worse than one that is off.]]></Comment><BitSize>273344</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_ControlModuleBase</ExtendsType><SubItem><Name>ParCfg</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_DigitalInputParCfg</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>265472</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ParCmd</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_DigitalInputParCmd</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>265536</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>OutCmd</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_DigitalInputOutCmd</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>265544</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>OutImm</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_DigitalInputOutImm</Type><BitSize>664</BitSize><BitOffs>265552</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_hal</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules" ReferenceTo="true">ST_DigitalInputHal</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>266240</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>OPC.UA.DA</Name><Value>0</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_identity</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_IoPointIdentity</Type><BitSize>6680</BitSize><BitOffs>266304</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_debounce</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ runs while the HAL value differs from the published Value]]></Comment><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>273024</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>DI_DEBOUNCE_MAX</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>273280</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#10S</DateTime></Default></SubItem><Method><Name>ConfigureIoIdentity</Name><Parameter><Name>Identity</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_IoPointIdentity</Type><BitSize>6680</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_ParCfgValid</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8/§5.6 - the layout this type was compiled against, and a debounce short
 enough to be a filter rather than a delay. Anything else is refused, never
 clamped. The DUT's own initializer is the layout version, so it is stated once.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>compiled</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_DigitalInputParCfg</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>Setup</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Name</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>HalRef</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules" ReferenceTo="true">ST_DigitalInputHal</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>DisplayNameKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>DescriptionKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>OnCyclic</Name><ReturnType>DINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>_M_Dispatch</Name></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_AirPressureHal</Name><BitSize>24</BitSize><SubItem><Name>LowPressure</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>OperatingPressure</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>8</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Quality</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>16</BitOffs><Default><Bool>true</Bool></Default></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_AirPressureParCfg</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ v2 moved ConflictTime to ST_AirPressureStationCfg: it varies per
 deployment, not per model, and §3.8a places such a value in station
 configuration. This monitor has no model data of its own, so what remains
 is the versioned shell the §3.12 contract asks every module to carry.]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><SubItem><Name>SchemaVersion</Name><Type>UINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8: MUST remain first]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs><Default><Value>2</Value></Default></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_AirPressureParCmd</Name><BitSize>8</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Reserved</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ passive monitor: physical four-structure contract, no command payload]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_AirPressureOutCmd</Name><BitSize>8</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Reserved</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ passive monitor: no command result]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_AirPressureOutImm</Name><BitSize>1336</BitSize><SubItem><Name>LowPressure</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>OperatingPressure</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>8</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>PressureOk</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>16</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Contradictory</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>24</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Quality</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>LowSensorTag</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>40</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>OperatingSensorTag</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>688</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_AirPressureStationCfg</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §3.8a/§3.8b — deployment data for this monitor. The qualification time
 depends on the physical switches and the air system they sit in, not on the
 product being made, so it is station configuration and NOT part of any model
 recipe: it must not change at changeover, and it must survive a restart.
 SchemaVersion stays first (§3.8b) so a retained image from another layout is
 rejected and re-initialized instead of read by field position.]]></Comment><BitSize>64</BitSize><SubItem><Name>SchemaVersion</Name><Type>UINT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs><Default><Value>1</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ConflictTime</Name><Type>TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ qualify contradictory mechanical switches]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#500MS</DateTime></Default></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_AirPressureMonitorCM</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Basic passive two-threshold pneumatic-pressure CM. Both switches active is
