t></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_AnalogInputHal</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ HAL boundary for one analog input channel. The composition root maps the
 raw process value here; identity is injected separately (S10.2.1).]]></Comment><BitSize>128</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Raw</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Quality</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Default><Bool>true</Bool></Default></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_AnalogInputCommand</Name><BitSize>32</BitSize><BaseType>DINT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>NONE</Text><Enum>0</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>MEASURE</Text><Enum>1</Enum></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>qualified_only</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_AnalogInputParCmd</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core S3.12 - the command parameter block. MEASURE has no parameter: the
 accepted window is ParCfg's (band, time, timeout), so the struct exists to
 keep the contract shape, not to carry a value.]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Reserved</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_AnalogInputOutCmd</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core S3.12 - the MEASURE result, valid on Done.]]></Comment><BitSize>64</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Value</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ the measured value]]></Comment><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_AnalogInputOutImm</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core S3.12 - cyclic status. Value is the filtered, tared engineering
 value; Gross (before tare) and Raw are published beside it because they are
 the adjustment's and the tare's capture sources (S3.8c(b)): the operator
 sees the number that is about to be stored.]]></Comment><BitSize>896</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Value</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Gross</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Raw</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Valid</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>192</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>InRange</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>200</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Stable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>208</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>IoTag</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>216</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_AnalogInputStationCfg</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core S3.8a/S3.8b - the installed sensor's two-point adjustment and tare:
 deployment data, retained across a restart, never part of a model recipe.
 An adjustment is ACTIVE when both references and both measured points
 differ; single points may be written while the pair is inactive, so an
 operator captures one point at a time. SchemaVersion first (S3.8b):
 0 = never written, 1 = this layout.]]></Comment><BitSize>384</BitSize><SubItem><Name>SchemaVersion</Name><Type>UINT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Ref1</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Ref2</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Meas1</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>192</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Meas2</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>256</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Tare</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>320</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_AnalogInputCM</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Generic analog-input CM: one type covering a plain signal, a measuring
 sensor (a value read once it is stable) and a scale (a tared reading) -
 the differences are configuration, not types (S1.1 O9). Scaling, the
 two-point adjustment, tare and a first-order filter are computed here, at
 the signal's owner (S7.2.1), so no sequence re-derives engineering units.
 Bad quality, a configuration the type cannot honour, or an implausible
 retained adjustment publishes Valid FALSE and Value 0 (S5.6) - never the
 last good value, which would be a measurement nobody made.]]></Comment><BitSize>275328</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_ControlModuleBase</ExtendsType><SubItem><Name>Command</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_AnalogInputCommand</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>265472</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ParCfg</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_AnalogInputParCfg</Type><BitSize>704</BitSize><BitOffs>265536</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ParCmd</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_AnalogInputParCmd</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>266240</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>OutCmd</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_AnalogInputOutCmd</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>266304</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>OutImm</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_AnalogInputOutImm</Type><BitSize>896</BitSize><BitOffs>266368</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_hal</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules" ReferenceTo="true">ST_AnalogInputHal</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>267264</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>OPC.UA.DA</Name><Value>0</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_identity</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_IoPointIdentity</Type><BitSize>6680</BitSize><BitOffs>267328</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_filtered</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ first-order filter state on Gross - Tare]]></Comment><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>274048</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_lastMs</Name><Type>TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TIME() of the previous valid scan, for dt]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>274112</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_primed</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ FALSE until the first valid sample primes filter and anchor]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>274144</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_anchor</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ stability reference; re-anchored on a band exit]]></Comment><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>274176</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_tStable</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>274240</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_tMeasure</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>274496</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>StationCfg</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_AnalogInputStationCfg</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ S3.8a/S3.8b - deployment data: the adjustment and tare belong to the
 installed sensor, not to any model recipe. The Setup registration, not
 this declaration, is what permits a write (S3.10.2).]]></Comment><BitSize>384</BitSize><BitOffs>274752</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>TcPersistent</Name></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>AI_STATIONCFG_SCHEMA</Name><Type>UINT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>275136</BitOffs><Default><Value>1</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>AI_FILTER_MAX</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>275168</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#10S</DateTime></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>AI_GAIN_MIN</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ adjustment gain vs nominal, plausible band]]></Comment><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>275200</BitOffs><Default><Value>0.5</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>AI_GAIN_MAX</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>275264</BitOffs><Default><Value>2</Value></Default></SubItem><Method><Name>ConfigureIoIdentity</Name><Parameter><Name>Identity</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_IoPointIdentity</Type><BitSize>6680</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_ParCfgValid</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ S3.8/S5.6 - the layout this type was compiled against, ranges that define
 a function, and a filter that is a filter rather than a delay. Anything
 else is refused, never clamped. The DUT's own initializer is the layout
 version, so it is stated once.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>compiled</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_AnalogInputParCfg</Type><BitSize>704</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_AdjustmentPlausible</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The retained pair is plausible when its gain lies within [AI_GAIN_MIN,
 AI_GAIN_MAX] of the nominal gain. The RATIO is compared, not its absolute
 value, so a reversed sign is implausible too. A pair outside the band is
 not a calibration; it is what a corrupted restore or a layout change
 leaves behind, and measuring through it would publish a number nobody
 calibrated.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Ref1</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Ref2</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Meas1</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Meas2</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>nominal</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>adjusted</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>ratio</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>Setup</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Name</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>HalRef</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules" ReferenceTo="true">ST_AnalogInputHal</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>DisplayNameKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>DescriptionKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>engLo</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>engHi</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>rawLo</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>rawHi</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>tareLim</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>OnCyclic</Name><ReturnType>DINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>cfgOk</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>active</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>plausible</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>valid</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>inRange</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>stable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>x</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>elapsedMs</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>now</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_Dispatch</Name><Local><Name>implausible</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_OnConfigWrite</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ S3.10.2 - a ref*/meas* candidate that would make the pair ACTIVE and
 implausible is refused here; anything that leaves the pair inactive is
 accepted, so an operator can write or capture one point at a time. This
 sees the RAW text and has no side effects: a non-number parses to 0 and is
 judged by the same rule, and the framework's own type check still rejects
 it after this returns TRUE. Captured candidates arrive by the same path.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>WriteKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>TextValue</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>ref1</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>ref2</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>meas1</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>meas2</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>candidate</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_AnalogInputCM_Tests</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Generic analog-input CM rows. T1/T4 are proven once in FB_Base_Tests; these
