 over [RawMin, RawMax] <- [EngMin, EngMax] (both ranges may be inverted);
 [Minimum, Maximum] is the band a SET target is accepted in, and SafeValue
 is what the channel drives whenever nothing is applied: before the first
 SET, while held, withdrawn, suspended or aborted (S5.6 - a channel whose
 state nobody stands behind drives the safe value, never the last one).]]></Comment><BitSize>576</BitSize><SubItem><Name>SchemaVersion</Name><Type>UINT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs><Default><Value>1</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>RawMin</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Default><Value>0</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>RawMax</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs><Default><Value>32767</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>EngMin</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>192</BitOffs><Default><Value>0</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>EngMax</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>256</BitOffs><Default><Value>100</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>UnitCode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_EngUnit</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>320</BitOffs><Default><EnumText>E_EngUnit.NONE</EnumText></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Minimum</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>384</BitOffs><Default><Value>0</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Maximum</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>448</BitOffs><Default><Value>100</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SafeValue</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>512</BitOffs><Default><Value>0</Value></Default></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_AnalogOutputHal</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ HAL boundary for one analog output channel. The composition root maps the
