 ends of the scaling. Withdrawn is the owner's functional stop (the same
 latch the cylinder publishes); a suspended channel (S9.3) drives SafeValue
 without setting Withdrawn, so the two states stay distinguishable.]]></Comment><BitSize>832</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Value</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Raw</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Withdrawn</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>IoTag</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>136</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_AnalogOutputStationCfg</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core S3.8a/S3.8b - the target a manual SET uses (the HMI's operator set
 point): deployment data, never part of a model recipe. SchemaVersion first
 (S3.8b): 0 = never written, 1 = this layout.]]></Comment><BitSize>128</BitSize><SubItem><Name>SchemaVersion</Name><Type>UINT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ManualTarget</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_AnalogOutputCM</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Generic analog-output CM. One command, SET, drives the channel to a target
 inside [ParCfg.Minimum, ParCfg.Maximum] and the value then stays applied
 until the next SET. Whatever state nobody stands behind drives SafeValue:
 before the first SET, while an interlock withholds it (S6.1 HELD during the
 command, no self-resume after Done - S9.3), while withdrawn by the owner's
 functional stop, and after an abort. Not a certified safe output; the
 safety system remains authoritative.]]></Comment><BitSize>316544</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_ControlModuleBase</ExtendsType><SubItem><Name>Command</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_AnalogOutputCommand</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>265472</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ParCfg</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_AnalogOutputParCfg</Type><BitSize>576</BitSize><BitOffs>265536</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ParCmd</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_AnalogOutputParCmd</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>266112</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>OutCmd</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_AnalogOutputOutCmd</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>266176</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>OutImm</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_AnalogOutputOutImm</Type><BitSize>832</BitSize><BitOffs>266240</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Intlk</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_PermIntlk</Type><BitSize>40320</BitSize><BitOffs>267072</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_hal</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules" ReferenceTo="true">ST_AnalogOutputHal</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>307392</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>OPC.UA.DA</Name><Value>0</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_identity</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_IoPointIdentity</Type><BitSize>6680</BitSize><BitOffs>307456</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_areaSafe</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ S7.2.1 - the application's area/process permit]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>314136</BitOffs><Default><Bool>true</Bool></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_areaSafeKey</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize><BitOffs>314144</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_withdrawn</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ WithdrawOutputs latch: until restore or the next SET]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>316192</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_suspended</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ interlock lost after Done: SafeValue, no self-resume (S9.3)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>316200</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_applied</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ a SET has completed and its value is held]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>316208</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_value</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ the applied engineering value]]></Comment><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>316224</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_useManualTarget</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ this SET came through ManualCommand]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>316288</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>StationCfg</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_AnalogOutputStationCfg</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ S3.8a/S3.8b - the operator's manual set point: deployment data, editable
 from the HMI, retained across a restart, never part of a model recipe.]]></Comment><BitSize>128</BitSize><BitOffs>316352</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>TcPersistent</Name></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>AO_STATIONCFG_SCHEMA</Name><Type>UINT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>316480</BitOffs><Default><Value>1</Value></Default></SubItem><Method><Name>WithdrawOutputs</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Functional stop used by an owning sequence: the channel drives SafeValue
 and stays there until RestoreOutputs or the next SET. This is not a
 certified stop; the safety system remains authoritative.]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>_M_ParCfgValid</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ S3.8/S5.6 - the layout this type was compiled against, a scaling that is a
 function, a band the channel can actually reach, and a safe value inside
 that band. Anything else is refused, never clamped.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>compiled</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_AnalogOutputParCfg</Type><BitSize>576</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>engLo</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>engHi</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>OnAbort</Name><ReturnType>DINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>Setup</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Name</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>HalRef</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules" ReferenceTo="true">ST_AnalogOutputHal</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>DisplayNameKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>DescriptionKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>SetAreaSafe</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core S7.2/S7.2.1 - the application supplies this type's area/process
 interlock, the same shape as FB_CylinderCM.SetAreaSafe: a method (not an
 OPC UA write), and the condition is re-evaluated every scan so a manual
 command obeys the same rule. Defaults TRUE: a station that declares no
 area interlock is not gated by one.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Ok</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>DescriptionKey</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>RestoreOutputs</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Symmetric counterpart to WithdrawOutputs. Re-asserts ONLY what the module
 itself would drive, and ONLY while the interlock permits it: a suspended
 channel (S9.3) is released, a withdrawn one re-applies its held value, and
 a channel with nothing applied keeps driving SafeValue. Idempotent; safe
 to call every scan. Not a certified enable - the safety system remains
 authoritative (S9).]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>_M_Dispatch</Name><Local><Name>target</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>d</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</Type><BitSize>5568</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>OnCyclic</Name><ReturnType>DINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>drive</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>ConfigureIoIdentity</Name><Parameter><Name>Identity</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_IoPointIdentity</Type><BitSize>6680</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_ScaleToRaw</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ One place states the channel's engineering-to-raw rule. Only called under
 a valid ParCfg (the division is guarded by the caller's check).]]></Comment><ReturnType>LREAL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>64</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Value</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_AnalogOutputCM_Tests</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Generic analog-output CM rows. T1/T4 are proven once in FB_Base_Tests; a
 one-scan command needs no timed rows, so one shared instance serves the
 rows that start clean, and dedicated instances cover the stateful ones
