 per curve by FB_CurveMonitor.M_Record: what was measured, what it was judged
 against and the verdict. The generic HMI reads it on demand for its Curve tab.
 Samples keeps the first PL_Curve.MAX_SAMPLES points; later ones were still
 judged (Result.Samples counts them all) and only Truncated says they are missing.]]></Comment><BitSize>43392</BitSize><SubItem><Name>SampleCount</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Truncated</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>16</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Samples</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_CurvePoint</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>256</Elements></ArrayInfo><BitSize>32768</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Spec</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_CurveSpec</Type><BitSize>9728</BitSize><BitOffs>32832</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Result</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_CurveResult</Type><BitSize>832</BitSize><BitOffs>42560</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_CurveMonitor</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The verdict on ONE measured curve - force over stroke, pressure over time -
 judged against windows the curve must pass through and envelopes it must
 stay on one side of. Owner-private, like FB_ValveDrive: no module identity,
 no published state, no I/O, and it raises nothing. The owner validates the
 spec in PrepareRecipe (M_Validate; refuse with CURVE_SPEC_INVALID), calls
 M_Begin when the curve starts, M_Sample once per measured point and
 M_Finish when it ends, then decides what a NOK means: a fault
 (_M_FaultN(Result.Reason, Result.DescriptionKey)) or a part verdict.

 Every rule is decided as the samples arrive, O(windows + envelopes) per
 sample, so the verdict needs no sample buffer. A window is judged on its
 samples: a curve sampled too sparsely to land one inside it misses it. The
 first PL_Curve.MAX_SAMPLES samples are kept only so M_Record can publish what
 was measured.]]></Comment><BitSize>43968</BitSize><SubItem><Name>_spec</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_CurveSpec</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ copied at M_Begin: a recipe committed mid-curve cannot move this verdict]]></Comment><BitSize>9728</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_specOk</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>9792</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_active</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ between M_Begin and M_Finish]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>9800</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_result</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_CurveResult</Type><BitSize>832</BitSize><BitOffs>9824</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_reach</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ the X a complete curve reaches]]></Comment><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>10688</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_maxX</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>10752</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_lastX</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>10816</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_lastY</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>10880</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_hasLast</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>10944</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_inside</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>4</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ the previous sample was inside window i]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>10952</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_seen</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>4</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ some sample was inside window i]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>10984</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_broken</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>4</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ window i was crossed through a wrong edge]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>11016</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_seg</Name><Type>INT</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>2</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ each envelope's current segment]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>11056</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_kept</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ samples kept for the record]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>11088</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_truncated</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ a sample arrived after the buffer filled]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>11104</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_samples</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_CurvePoint</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>256</Elements></ArrayInfo><BitSize>32768</BitSize><BitOffs>11136</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_finished</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ a curve has finished since the last M_Begin]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>43904</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>_M_EntryEdge</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The edge the segment from the previous (outside) sample to (X, Y) (inside)
 enters window Index through: of the bounds the previous sample violates, the
 one crossed LAST (largest segment parameter). An exact corner goes to the
 first in LEFT, RIGHT, BOTTOM, TOP order. Every divisor is non-zero: the
 previous sample lies strictly beyond the bound and (X, Y) on or inside it.]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_CurveEdge</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>16</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Index</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>X</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Y</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>w</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules" ReferenceTo="true">ST_CurveWindow</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>t</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>best</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_ExitEdge</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The edge the segment from the previous (inside) sample to (X, Y) (outside)
 leaves window Index through: of the bounds (X, Y) violates, the one crossed
 FIRST (smallest segment parameter); ties as in _M_EntryEdge.]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_CurveEdge</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>16</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Index</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>X</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Y</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>w</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules" ReferenceTo="true">ST_CurveWindow</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>t</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>best</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_EdgeKnown</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Edge</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_CurveEdge</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_Begin</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Start a curve: the spec is validated and copied, the previous curve forgotten.
