 every window a real rectangle with known edges, every envelope at least two
 points with X strictly increasing. The owner refuses anything else at
 PrepareRecipe, so it never reaches a curve as behaviour.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Spec</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules" ReferenceTo="true">ST_CurveSpec</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>k</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_EnvelopeCut</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE when (X, Y) lies on the wrong side of envelope Index (linear
 interpolation; outside the envelope's X span nothing is judged). The segment
 cursor moves with X, so a monotonic curve costs O(1) per sample.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Index</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>X</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Y</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>e</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules" ReferenceTo="true">ST_CurveEnvelope</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>k</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>n</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>bound</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_Finish</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ End the curve and return its verdict. OK only when complete, every window
 passed and no envelope cut; otherwise NOK with the first failing rule.
 Calling it again returns the same result; samples after it are ignored.]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_CurveResult</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>832</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>windowsOk</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_Record</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Copy the last FINISHED curve into the owner's published record (once per
 curve, after M_Finish): the kept samples, the spec it was judged against and
 the verdict. Refused (FALSE, Target untouched) while a curve runs or before
 the first one finishes, so a record never shows half a curve. Rows past
 SampleCount are cleared, and a curve judged against an invalid spec is
