 Returns 0 when no corridor is legal - a one-way nest asked to reverse.]]></Comment><ReturnType>INT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>16</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Gripper</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Nest</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>OtherRegion</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Dir</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_HelpRole</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>_i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>_n</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>_cand</Name><Type>INT</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>4</Elements></ArrayInfo><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>_first</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>__Index__0</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_RegionOf</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The transit region of the move's other endpoint, used only to break ties
 between same-direction corridors. A help carries its region directly; a nest
 borrows the region of its first serving help.]]></Comment><ReturnType>DWORD</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Gripper</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Nest</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Help</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>_h</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_ValidEnds</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Exactly one of Nest/Help at each end, and every index in range (S5.6).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Gripper</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>FromNest</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>FromHelp</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ToNest</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ToHelp</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_RobotPlanner_Tests</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Annex I I.9-I.10.2 route planner, against the geometry of the reviewed cell.

 The fixture is deliberately the real thing rather than a toy: five help
 points, the twelve work positions of a plasma-clean handling cell, and the
 scan position that sits between two transit regions - reachable from the
 drawer side via HELP4 and the process side via HELP5. That junction is the
 case the reference framework could not express declaratively and hand-coded
 in two different methods from private state; if the affinity table cannot
 reproduce it in BOTH directions with no branching, the model has failed and
 it is better to find out here than in an annex.

 No arm, no connector, no motion: the planner is pure logic (S5.7, Annex H).]]></Comment><BitSize>34614272</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="TcUnit">FB_TestSuite</ExtendsType><SubItem><Name>HELP1</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ change-position side]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>33574912</BitOffs><Default><Value>1</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>HELP2</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ left drawer]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>33574928</BitOffs><Default><Value>2</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>HELP3</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ home / NIO drawer]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>33574944</BitOffs><Default><Value>3</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>HELP4</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ drawer-side scan approach]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>33574960</BitOffs><Default><Value>4</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>HELP5</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ process side]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>33574976</BitOffs><Default><Value>5</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>CP_GRIPPER1</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ nests]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>33574992</BitOffs><Default><Value>1</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>READ_GRIPPER</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>33575008</BitOffs><Default><Value>2</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SCAN_PART</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>33575024</BitOffs><Default><Value>3</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>DRAWER_LEFT</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>33575040</BitOffs><Default><Value>4</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>DRAWER_RIGHT</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>33575056</BitOffs><Default><Value>5</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>DRAWER_NIO</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>33575072</BitOffs><Default><Value>6</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>PROCESS_START</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>33575088</BitOffs><Default><Value>7</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ONE_WAY_NEST</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ synthetic: entry-only, to prove the loud refusal]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>33575104</BitOffs><Default><Value>8</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ISLAND_NEST</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ synthetic: served by a help with no graph edge]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>33575120</BitOffs><Default><Value>9</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>REGION_DRAWER</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ transit regions]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>33575136</BitOffs><Default><Value>1</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>REGION_PROCESS</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>33575168</BitOffs><Default><Value>2</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>G_WITH</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ a gripper is coupled - tall approach]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>33575200</BitOffs><Default><Value>1</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>G_NONE</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ nothing coupled - short approach]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>33575216</BitOffs><Default><Value>2</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_graph</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_RouteGraph</Type><BitSize>996096</BitSize><BitOffs>33575232</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_geom</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_RobotGeometry</Type><BitSize>27648</BitSize><BitOffs>34571328</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_p</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_RobotRoutePlanner</Type><BitSize>704</BitSize><BitOffs>34598976</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_route</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_RobotPointList</Type><BitSize>14400</BitSize><BitOffs>34599680</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_ret</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>34614080</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_help</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>34614112</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_built</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>34614128</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_w1</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>34614136</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_w2</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>34614144</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_w3</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>34614152</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_w4</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>34614160</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_w5</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>34614168</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_w6</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>34614176</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_w7</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>34614184</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_w8</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>34614192</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_w9</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>34614200</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_w10</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>34614208</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>Direct_nest_list_bypasses_help_routing</Name></Method><Method><Name>_M_FindAffinity</Name><ReturnType>INT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>16</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Gripper</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Nest</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>HelpId</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>_i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>Scan_junction_resolves_the_process_side_help</Name></Method><Method><Name>_M_Affinity1</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ One nest served by one help, both directions, offsets unset.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Gripper</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Nest</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>HelpId</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_BuildFixture</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The reviewed cell as configuration - which is the whole point: a station
 supplies a table, not traversal code.]]></Comment><Local><Name>_i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>Taught_corridor_emits_a_list_reference_instead_of_offsets</Name><Local><Name>_i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>Malformed_endpoints_are_rejected_before_planning</Name></Method><Method><Name>_M_Corridor2</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ A two-step corridor - the reference's "back out, then lift" retract.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Gripper</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Nest</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>HelpId</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>D1X</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>D1Y</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>D1Z</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>D2X</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>D2Y</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>D2Z</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>_i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_Corridor1</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ A one-step corridor, used for both approach and depart.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Gripper</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Nest</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>HelpId</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>DX</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>DY</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>DZ</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>_i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>Nest_to_nest_emits_depart_then_transit_then_approach</Name></Method><Method><Name>One_way_nest_refuses_the_reversal_loudly</Name></Method><Method><Name>Approach_corridor_is_reversed_and_lands_exactly_on_the_nest</Name></Method><Method><Name>Corridor_differs_per_gripper_with_no_conditional_code</Name></Method><Method><Name>Disconnected_graph_yields_ROBOT_NO_ROUTE</Name></Method><Method><Name>Scan_junction_resolves_the_drawer_side_help_in_the_same_table</Name></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotOpMode</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Annex I I.4a(a) - the robot CONTROLLER's operating mode, which bounds what
 motion is physically allowed. The PLC REQUESTS a mode and publishes separately
 what the controller REPORTS it actually is: a request that was not granted must
 stay visibly ungranted, never overwritten by optimism. UNKNOWN = 0 so an
 uninitialised value is never mistaken for a permissive mode.]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BaseType>DINT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>UNKNOWN</Text><Enum>0</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>AUTO_REMOTE</Text><Enum>1</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>MANUAL_REDUCED</Text><Enum>2</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>MANUAL_HIGH</Text><Enum>3</Enum></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>qualified_only</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_RobotCapabilities</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Annex I I.3 - what the CONNECTED controller says it offers, as its connector
 reports it. Facts, never configuration: the robot CM refuses a command the
 controller does not offer before anything is sent, and bounds jog axes and
 user signals by what it carries. Reported = FALSE means the controller has
 not said (not linked yet, or a server that predates the question): nothing
 is filtered then, and the controller's own refusal stays the authority.]]></Comment><BitSize>192</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Reported</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Commands</Name><Type>LWORD</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ bit n set = E_RobotCommand value n is offered]]></Comment><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>JogAxes</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ axes a jog may address, additional axes included; 0 = no jog]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>UserSignals</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ user-signal slots the robot program exchanges (I.3)]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>144</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotJogMode</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Annex I I.3 - jog frame for manual motion. Named E_RobotJogMode, not
 E_JogMode: the short name collides with a Beckhoff motion-library type and the
 ambiguity surfaces only in a consumer that references both. Manual only, release-gated (S7.6).]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BaseType>DINT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>JOINT</Text><Enum>0</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>CARTESIAN</Text><Enum>1</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>TOOL</Text><Enum>2</Enum></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>qualified_only</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">I_RobotConnector</Name><BitSize>64</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_DeviceConnector</ExtendsType><Method><Name>__getActualMode</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ What the controller REPORTS its operating mode to be - read-only status, and
 never treated as a safety grant (S9). Deliberately separate from the request.]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotOpMode</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getActualPosition</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ SRCI ReadActualPosition (Core). Live TCP pose, for display and diagnostics.
 Reading a pose is not commanding one, so I.1's boundary is untouched.]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_RobotPose</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>384</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getArmPowerOn</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ NO SRCI EQUIVALENT ASSERTED. The controller REPORTS its drives powered. Read-only
 status (I.4): a safety-alias loss drops power through PowerOff, and nothing
 re-enables it but a deliberate POWER_ON (S9.3/S9.4).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getCapabilities</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ NO SRCI EQUIVALENT ASSERTED. What the connected controller says it offers.
 Reported = FALSE until it has said; an unreported set filters nothing.]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_RobotCapabilities</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>192</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getControllerMessage</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ SRCI ReadMessages (Core). The robot's OWN message, carried verbatim - what a
 service technician actually needs, rather than a Fraktal paraphrase.]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>5568</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getCurrentArea</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ NO SRCI EQUIVALENT. The planning area the TCP is in; 0 = none/undefined, which
 is what makes ROBOT_AREA_UNRESOLVED an explicit first-out instead of a silent
 stall (I.11).]]></Comment><ReturnType>DWORD</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getLastResult</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ First-out reason and SourcePath of the last refused or failed request, adopted
 verbatim by the owning CM's rollup (S8.2).]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>5568</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getMotionBusy</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The ROBOT is executing motion. Deliberately NOT called Busy: the module base
 already publishes Busy for its own command handshake, and the two are different
 questions - "is my command running" versus "is the arm moving".]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getPathIndex</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ NO SRCI EQUIVALENT ASSERTED. The index of the last point of the current or most
 recent RUN_PATH the robot has COMPLETED; -1 = none. After an abort it says where
 the path stopped, so a deliberate RUN_PATH from PathIndex + 1 continues it - from
 wherever the arm stands, never automatically (Annex D / S9.3).]]></Comment><ReturnType>DINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getProtectiveStop</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ NO SRCI EQUIVALENT. Collision/crash-protection device tripped. This is PROCESS
 protection, detected and acted on by the ordinary PLC - NOT a S9 safety
 function, and deliberately carrying its own reason so the alarm record does not
 misreport a process event as a safety event (I.4a(c)).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getReferenced</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ A valid home/reference exists. MOVE/RUN before this is refused (S5.6).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getResumable</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ NO SRCI EQUIVALENT. Whether Resume is still valid on the retained path. A hold
 is exactly the window in which an operator is most likely to jog the arm - that
 is what the pause was for - so this turns "the arm was moved while suspended"
 into a clean refusal instead of a move through untaught space (I.4b).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>Abort</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ SRCI GroupStop (Core). Commands are NOT auto-repeated; resumption is
 deliberate (Annex D / S9.3).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>Home</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ SRCI referencing. Drive to the home/reference configuration.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>Interrupt</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ SRCI GroupInterrupt (Core). Stop ON PATH, retaining the resume point - the
 robot half of the S6.1 HELD contract (I.4b). A cylinder honours HELD by
 de-energising; a robot cannot, because resuming a 26-point path by
 re-commanding it would re-run executed points or approach from an untaught pose.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>Jog</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ SRCI GroupJog (Core). Manual only, release-gated (S7.6), and refused unless
 ActualMode is a manual mode (I.4a(a)).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Mode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotJogMode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Axis</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Dir</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>MoveFromArea</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ NO SRCI EQUIVALENT. Route planned from WHICHEVER planning area the TCP
 currently occupies, resolved live. The application's primary motion command,
 because it needs no assumption about the start pose; pose recovery after an
 E-stop is its extreme case, not a separate mode (I.11).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>ToPosId</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>MoveTemplate</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ NO SRCI EQUIVALENT. Route generated by the declarative help/nest graph between
 two KNOWN positions (I.9) - the PLC names from and to, never the waypoints.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>FromPosId</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ToPosId</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>MoveToPoint</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ SRCI MoveDirectAbsolute/MoveLinearAbsolute, target resolved from the ID.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>PointId</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>PowerOff</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ SRCI EnableRobot (Core). Arm power off.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>PowerOn</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ SRCI EnableRobot (Core). Arm power on.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>RequestMode</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ SRCI SetOperationMode (Core). REQUEST only - the controller grants. Compare
 with ActualMode, which reports what it actually is (I.4a(a)).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Mode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotOpMode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>ResetController</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ SRCI GroupReset (Core). Acknowledge the robot's OWN messages. Without this a
 controller fault can be detected but never cleared.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>Resume</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ SRCI GroupContinue (Core). Continue FROM the retained path point. Callers
 must check Resumable first: resuming onto a path the tool has left is how a
 robot drives through a fixture (I.4b).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>RunPallet</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ NO SRCI EQUIVALENT. One nest of a generated pallet grid, addressed by pallet
 ID and nest index; the grid itself is generated from taught corners (I.12).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>PalletId</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Nest</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>RunPath</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Sequential SRCI moves over a stored list. (-1,-1) = the whole list.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>ListId</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>StartIdx</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>EndIdx</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>SetFrame</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ SRCI ReadFrameData (Core) - selection by ID. The frame may be chained (I.12).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>FrameId</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>SetPayload</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ SRCI Read/WriteLoadData. The active load case, which changes the moment a part
 is gripped or released; a move computed for the wrong mass degrades accuracy
 and brake margin silently (I.3).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>LoadId</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>SetSpeedScale</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ SRCI ChangeSpeedOverride (Core). Ceiling on path speed, as a percentage of
 taught. The CM applies MIN(mode ceiling, recipe scale) (I.4a(b)).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Percent</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>SetTool</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ SRCI ReadToolData (Core) - selection by ID. Geometry stays taught data.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>ToolId</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>UserSignal</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ NO SRCI EQUIVALENT ASSERTED. The last value the robot program reported for
 user signal Index; 0 when out of range or never reported. Valid only while
 Linked - the owning CM publishes that alongside.]]></Comment><ReturnType>LREAL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>64</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Index</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>WriteUserSignal</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ NO SRCI EQUIVALENT ASSERTED. Hand one declared to-robot user signal to the
 robot program (I.3 user channel). Level semantics: the value stands until the
 next write and is re-sent after a reconnect. FALSE = not linked or index out
 of range. Data, never a command - positions, modes and "go" stay ID-addressed.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Index</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Value</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceId</Name><Value>4375</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">I_RobotRoutines</Name><BitSize>64</BitSize><ExtendsType>IQueryInterface</ExtendsType><Method><Name>__getBrakeTestDue</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The controller asks for its brake test.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getSafeReferenceDue</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The controller asks for its safe reference run.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>RunBrakeTest</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Start the controller's brake test. FALSE = refused, with the connector's
 LastResult carrying the reason (I.3).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>RunSafeReference</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Start the controller's safe reference run; as RunBrakeTest.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceId</Name><Value>4415</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_StaubliConnParCfg</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Deployment configuration for the VAL3 connector (S3.8a station config).]]></Comment><BitSize>800</BitSize><SubItem><Name>SchemaVersion</Name><Type>UINT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs><Default><Value>1</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Host</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>16</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Port</Name><Type>UINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ VAL3 fraktal_server command socket]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>672</BitOffs><Default><Value>11000</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Terminator</Name><Type>STRING(2)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ ASCII 13, as the Staubli sioLink default]]></Comment><BitSize>24</BitSize><BitOffs>688</BitOffs><Default><String>
</String></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>RespTimeout</Name><Type>TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ per-request; motion completion is polled, not awaited]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>736</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#2S</DateTime></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>StatusPeriod</Name><Type>TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ idle status poll interval]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>768</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#100MS</DateTime></Default></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_StaubliVal3Connector</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Annex I I.3/I.5 - Staubli VAL3 connector: one conformant implementation of
 I_RobotConnector, speaking a line protocol to a `fraktal_server` VAL3
 application on the robot controller.

 WHY TCP AND NOT uniVAL/EtherCAT. Both are conformant behind this interface and
 the parent Unit is unchanged either way (I.5), but only this one can be
 developed and regression-tested with NO ARM: the Staubli Robotics Suite
 Emulator answers the same TCP sockets as a real CS9 controller, whereas a
 virtual controller cannot present an EtherCAT slave. uniVAL plc over EtherCAT
 (Beckhoff TF5130) remains the production binding where cycle determinism
 matters; this one is what makes O6 - commissioning before hardware - true for
 a robot cell, and what S5.7 tests run against.

 A CONNECTOR, like FB_SimRobotConnector (Core §3.15.1): it is serviced by the
 robot CM it is composed in (§3.15.3), so swapping the two changes a declaration
 and not the module tree (I.5). Everything connector-shaped is INHERITED from
 FB_DeviceConnectorBase - session, heartbeat, loss confirmation after
 LinkTimeout, bounded reconnect with no self-resume (§3.15.2) - and the ASCII
 framing and one-outstanding-request rule are FB_AsciiLink's, shared with the
 device CMs (§1.1 O9). This type adds only the robot protocol.

 PROTOCOL (ASCII, one line per message, terminator from ParCfg):
   request   <CMD>[,<arg>]...
   response  <CMD>,OK[,<payload>]...   accepted / completed
             <CMD>,ERR,<code>,<text>   refused or faulted by the controller
   status    STA[,<out1>,...,<outN>]   the poll carries the to-robot user signals
             STA,OK,<busy>,<ref>,<mode>,<area>,<prot>,<resumable>,<x>,<y>,<z>,
                    <rx>,<ry>,<rz>,<power>,<pathIdx>,<due>,<in1>,...,<inN>
   <power>, <pathIdx>, <due> and the user values are appended fields: a server
   that predates them omits them, which reads as drives not reported powered, no
   path progress (-1), nothing due and inputs 0. <due> is a bit set: 1 = brake
   test due, 2 = safe reference run due. Riding
   the status poll costs the user channel no request slot of its own, so it can
   never refuse a motion command for being busy.
   offer     CAP -> CAP,OK,<commands>,<jogAxes>,<userSignals>, asked once per
             session; <commands> bit n = E_RobotCommand n. A server that answers
             ERR, or nothing, leaves the set unreported, which filters nothing.
   routines  BRK (brake test), SRF (safe reference run); completion and verdict
             through the poll (<busy>, <due>).
   refusal codes this connector classifies: UNKNOWN_ID (point, list or pallet not
             taught) -> ROBOT_POINT_UNKNOWN; any other -> ROBOT_CONTROLLER_FAULT.
             The controller's own text travels verbatim either way (S8.2).
 Commands are ID-ADDRESSED (I.1): a point, list, pallet, tool, frame or load is
 named by its identifier and never by a coordinate. The single exception the
 standard permits - a bounded offset correction for a runtime-located target
 (I.8a) - is not implemented here yet and is not smuggled in.

 ONE ON THE WIRE, TWO WAITING. The link allows one outstanding request, but the
 CM sends the speed and then the move in the same scan, and the heartbeat's STA
 (or the once-per-session CAP) can hold the slot at that very scan. Requests
 arriving while the slot is taken wait in a two-deep queue, oldest first, and go
 out as the replies land; only a third is refused. (One waiting place was not
 enough: with the poll on the wire the speed took it and the move was refused.)
 Abort empties the queue first, so a stop never sits behind the move it stops.

 STATUS IS THE HEARTBEAT: every ParCfg.StatusPeriod the connector issues STA, so
 MotionBusy/Referenced/ActualMode/CurrentArea/ProtectiveStop/Resumable/pose stay
 current without the robot originating traffic, and a controller that stops
 answering is declared lost after LinkTimeout rather than trusted forever.]]></Comment><BitSize>34304</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_DeviceConnectorBase</ExtendsType><Implements Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">I_RobotConnector</Implements><Implements Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">I_RobotRoutines</Implements><SubItem><Name>ParCfg</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_StaubliConnParCfg</Type><BitSize>800</BitSize><BitOffs>7552</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>LinkState</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ByteChannelState</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ the transport, for diagnosis]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>8352</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>LastResponse</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ the controller's last reply, verbatim]]></Comment><BitSize>2048</BitSize><BitOffs>8384</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_link</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_AsciiLink</Type><BitSize>6656</BitSize><BitOffs>10432</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>OPC.UA.DA</Name><Value>0</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_busy</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>17088</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_referenced</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>17096</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_mode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotOpMode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>17120</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_reqMode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotOpMode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>17152</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_area</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>17184</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_protStop</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>17216</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_resumable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>17224</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_pose</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_RobotPose</Type><BitSize>384</BitSize><BitOffs>17280</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_ctrlMsg</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</Type><BitSize>5568</BitSize><BitOffs>17664</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_lastResult</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</Type><BitSize>5568</BitSize><BitOffs>23232</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_statusPend</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ the outstanding request is the heartbeat's STA]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>28800</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_hbReply</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ a well-formed reply arrived since the heartbeat asked]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>28808</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_power</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ drives reported powered (STA field 15)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>28816</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_pathIdx</Name><Type>DINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ last completed path point (STA field 16); -1 = none]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>28832</BitOffs><Default><Value>-1</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_userIn</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>8</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ reported by the robot program]]></Comment><BitSize>512</BitSize><BitOffs>28864</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_userOut</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>8</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ handed to it with every poll]]></Comment><BitSize>512</BitSize><BitOffs>29376</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_userOutCount</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ highest to-robot index ever written; 0 = plain STA]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>29888</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_queue</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>2</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ requests waiting for the slot, oldest first]]></Comment><BitSize>4096</BitSize><BitOffs>29904</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_queued</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ how many are waiting (0..2)]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>34000</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_caps</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_RobotCapabilities</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ the controller's answer to CAP]]></Comment><BitSize>192</BitSize><BitOffs>34048</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_capAsked</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ CAP was sent on this session]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>34240</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_capPend</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ the outstanding request is CAP]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>34248</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_due</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ STA field 17: 1 = brake test due, 2 = safe reference due]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>34272</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>_M_StatusRequest</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The status poll, carrying every to-robot user value written so far: level
 semantics, re-sent each poll, so a reconnect restores them with no extra step.]]></Comment><ReturnType>STRING(255)</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>2048</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>__getResumable</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>Resumable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>Cyclic</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Run the link and parse what it delivered, then let the base run the session,
 the heartbeat and the bounded reconnect exactly as for any connector.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>evt</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_AsciiLinkEvent</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>RunPath</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>ListId</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>StartIdx</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>EndIdx</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>__getLastResult</Name><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>5568</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>LastResult</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</Type><BitSize>5568</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>RequestMode</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Mode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotOpMode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>_s</Name><Type>STRING(8)</Type><BitSize>72</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_HbPoll</Name><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_HbResult</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>MoveFromArea</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>ToPosId</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>__getBrakeTestDue</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>BrakeTestDue</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>WriteUserSignal</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Recorded and sent with the next status poll. Not a robot request: LastResult
 is left as it was, and no request slot is taken.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Index</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Value</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>SetTool</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>ToolId</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_HbStart</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The heartbeat IS the status poll. With a command reply still outstanding the
 slot is taken, so that reply is awaited instead: any well-formed reply proves the
 controller alive, and the one-outstanding-request rule is never broken by
 housekeeping.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>__getSafeReferenceDue</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>SafeReferenceDue</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>_M_MakeCtrlDiag</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Wrap the controller's own error into a Fraktal diagnostic without translating it.]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>5568</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Code</Name><Type>STRING(64)</Type><BitSize>520</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Text</Name><Type>STRING(64)</Type><BitSize>520</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_MakeLinkDiag</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The link is the reason a request was refused; reuse the Framework band rather
 than minting a robot code for a transport fact (Annex D).]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>5568</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>SetSpeedScale</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Percent</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>Interrupt</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>_M_Close</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>SetPayload</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>LoadId</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>RunSafeReference</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>__getActualMode</Name><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotOpMode</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>ActualMode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotOpMode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>SetFrame</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>FrameId</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_OnResponse</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Parse one terminated reply. Status replies refresh the published facts; command
 replies clear Busy or record the controller's own first-out.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Response</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>_cmd</Name><Type>STRING(16)</Type><BitSize>136</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>_stat</Name><Type>STRING(16)</Type><BitSize>136</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>UserSignal</Name><ReturnType>LREAL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>64</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Index</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_ToMode</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Controller mode text -> E_RobotOpMode. Anything unrecognised is UNKNOWN, never
 a permissive mode: an unparsed reply must not read as "auto is granted".]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotOpMode</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>ModeText</Name><Type>STRING(64)</Type><BitSize>520</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>MoveTemplate</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>FromPosId</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ToPosId</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>Abort</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>__getCurrentArea</Name><ReturnType>DWORD</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>CurrentArea</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>_M_Open</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>RunBrakeTest</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>__getMotionBusy</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The ROBOT is moving. The base already owns Busy for its own command handshake;
 conflating the two would make "is the arm moving" unanswerable.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>MotionBusy</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>RunPallet</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>PalletId</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Nest</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_Field</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ n-th comma-separated field of a response, 1-based; '' when absent. Bounded and
 allocation-free (O10).]]></Comment><ReturnType>STRING(64)</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>520</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Text</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>N</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>count</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>start</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>len_</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>ch</Name><Type>STRING(1)</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_Request</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Issue one ID-addressed request. FALSE = refused outright, with LastResult set,
 which is what the CM turns into a first-out (S5.6).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Text</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>Resume</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>PowerOn</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>PowerOff</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>Jog</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Mode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotJogMode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Axis</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Dir</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>MoveToPoint</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>PointId</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>__getReferenced</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>Referenced</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>SetupLink</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Wire identity and transport. Called once from the composition root (S3.11);
 the robot CM then services the connector every scan (§3.15.3).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Name</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Chan</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_ByteChannel</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>DevHost</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>DevPort</Name><Type>UINT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_Num</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ A user value on the wire: a whole number without a fraction (flags and
 integers are exact), anything else as LREAL text.]]></Comment><ReturnType>STRING(32)</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>264</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Value</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>ResetController</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>__getActualPosition</Name><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_RobotPose</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>384</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>ActualPosition</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_RobotPose</Type><BitSize>384</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getControllerMessage</Name><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>5568</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>ControllerMessage</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</Type><BitSize>5568</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getProtectiveStop</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>ProtectiveStop</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getPathIndex</Name><ReturnType>DINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>PathIndex</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getCapabilities</Name><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_RobotCapabilities</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>192</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>Capabilities</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_RobotCapabilities</Type><BitSize>192</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getArmPowerOn</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>ArmPowerOn</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>Home</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_RobotConnector_Tests</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Annex I I.3/I.5 - the Staubli VAL3 connector over the SIM channel. No socket,
 no emulator, no arm: FB_SimByteChannel scripts request/reply pairs, so the wire
 protocol and every refusal path are provable in CI (S5.7, Annex H).

 This is the transport-layer half of the I.5c simulation requirement. The SRS
 Emulator remains the higher-fidelity layer for motion behaviour; what is proven
 here is the part that must hold before an emulator is worth starting: that the
 connector speaks the agreed frames, and that it REFUSES rather than pretends
 when the link is down, the mode is wrong, or the path was left.

 Linked means session up AND heartbeat healthy (Core §3.15.2), and the heartbeat
 is the TON-driven status poll, so every test that needs a live link runs ACROSS
 SCANS and scripts the STA reply the heartbeat asks for.]]></Comment><BitSize>34206080</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="TcUnit">FB_TestSuite</ExtendsType><SubItem><Name>_chan</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_SimByteChannel</Type><BitSize>35072</BitSize><BitOffs>33574912</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_conn</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_StaubliVal3Connector</Type><BitSize>34304</BitSize><BitOffs>33609984</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_chanB</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_SimByteChannel</Type><BitSize>35072</BitSize><BitOffs>33644288</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_connB</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_StaubliVal3Connector</Type><BitSize>34304</BitSize><BitOffs>33679360</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_chanC</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_SimByteChannel</Type><BitSize>35072</BitSize><BitOffs>33713664</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_connC</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_StaubliVal3Connector</Type><BitSize>34304</BitSize><BitOffs>33748736</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_chanD</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_SimByteChannel</Type><BitSize>35072</BitSize><BitOffs>33783040</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_connD</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_StaubliVal3Connector</Type><BitSize>34304</BitSize><BitOffs>33818112</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_ok</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>33852416</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>33852432</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_i2</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>33852448</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_i4</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>33852464</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_diag</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ C0185: cannot access .member on a property result]]></Comment><BitSize>5568</BitSize><BitOffs>33852480</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_pose</Name><Type Namespace="Fr