hanG</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_SimByteChannel</Type><BitSize>35072</BitSize><BitOffs>33997376</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_connG</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_StaubliVal3Connector</Type><BitSize>34304</BitSize><BitOffs>34032448</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_iG</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>34066752</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_wG</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>34066768</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_sentG</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>34066776</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_chanH</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_SimByteChannel</Type><BitSize>35072</BitSize><BitOffs>34066816</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_connH</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_StaubliVal3Connector</Type><BitSize>34304</BitSize><BitOffs>34101888</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_iH</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>34136192</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_wH</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>34136208</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_capsH</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_RobotCapabilities</Type><BitSize>192</BitSize><BitOffs>34136256</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_chanI</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_SimByteChannel</Type><BitSize>35072</BitSize><BitOffs>34136448</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_connI</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_StaubliVal3Connector</Type><BitSize>34304</BitSize><BitOffs>34171520</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_iI</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>34205824</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_wI</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>34205840</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_sentI</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>34205848</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_capsI</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_RobotCapabilities</Type><BitSize>192</BitSize><BitOffs>34205888</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>Status_poll_publishes_the_controllers_reported_facts</Name></Method><Method><Name>An_untaught_point_is_refused_with_its_own_reason_and_an_unanswered_offer_filters_nothing</Name></Method><Method><Name>Resume_is_refused_when_the_arm_left_the_retained_path</Name></Method><Method><Name>Controller_error_is_carried_verbatim_and_faults</Name></Method><Method><Name>User_outputs_ride_the_status_poll</Name></Method><Method><Name>Status_reply_reports_arm_power_and_user_inputs</Name></Method><Method><Name>Link_down_refuses_every_command_rather_than_dropping_it</Name></Method><Method><Name>Unknown_mode_request_is_refused_outright</Name></Method><Method><Name>Id_addressed_commands_are_framed_on_the_wire</Name></Method><Method><Name>Speed_then_move_in_one_scan_both_reach_the_wire</Name></Method><Method><Name>The_controllers_offer_is_asked_once_and_its_demands_decoded</Name></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">I_SimulatedRobotConnector</Name><BitSize>64</BitSize><ExtendsType>IQueryInterface</ExtendsType><Method><Name>__getSimulated</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Explicit connector identity; empty marker interfaces are not sufficient.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotCommand</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Annex I I.4 - the robot CM's command vocabulary. A point, a taught path, a
 generated route or a pallet nest is ONE command that runs to completion, so the
 robot looks identical to any other CM (S6.1). IDs are the only addressing.]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BaseType>DINT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>NONE</Text><Enum>0</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>POWER_ON</Text><Enum>1</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>POWER_OFF</Text><Enum>2</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>HOME</Text><Enum>3</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>MOVE_TO</Text><Enum>4</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ one taught point, by ID]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>RUN_PATH</Text><Enum>5</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ a stored list, by ID and optional sub-range]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>RUN_PALLET</Text><Enum>6</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ one nest of a generated pallet grid]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>MOVE_TEMPLATE</Text><Enum>7</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ route generated by the help/nest graph (I.9)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>MOVE_FROM_AREA</Text><Enum>8</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ start resolved live from the current area (I.11)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>SET_TOOL</Text><Enum>9</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>SET_FRAME</Text><Enum>10</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>RECONNECT</Text><Enum>11</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.15.4 deliberate reconnect; never resumes a command]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>REQUEST_MODE</Text><Enum>12</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ ask the controller for ParCmd.Mode; Done when it REPORTS it (I.4a(a))]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>SET_PAYLOAD</Text><Enum>13</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ select the active load case by ID (ParCmd.TargetId), as SET_TOOL (I.3)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>JOG_POS</Text><Enum>14</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ HELD manual command only (RequestHeldCommand), never Execute (§7.6.1)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>JOG_NEG</Text><Enum>15</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>BRAKE_TEST</Text><Enum>16</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ run the controller's own brake test; passed when it withdraws its demand]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>SAFE_REFERENCE</Text><Enum>17</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ run the controller's own safe reference run; likewise]]></Comment></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>qualified_only</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotSignalKind</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Annex I I.3 - what a declared user signal holds. Every kind travels as an
 LREAL; the kind is what a write is checked against (0/1, a whole number).]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BaseType>DINT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>BOOL_SIGNAL</Text><Enum>0</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>INT_SIGNAL</Text><Enum>1</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>REAL_SIGNAL</Text><Enum>2</Enum></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>qualified_only</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_RobotParCfg</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Recipe-class configuration (S3.8), versioned.]]></Comment><BitSize>384</BitSize><SubItem><Name>SchemaVersion</Name><Type>UINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ v2 appended DefaultMode, ModeTimeout, JogTimeout]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs><Default><Value>2</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>MoveTimeout</Name><Type>TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ per-command guard; the Unit step's ExpectedTime (S6.5) remains the outer one]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#60S</DateTime></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>HomeTimeout</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#120S</DateTime></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SpeedScaleMin</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ band a recipe SpeedScale is validated against (I.4a(b))]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>96</BitOffs><Default><Value>1</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SpeedScaleMax</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs><Default><Value>100</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SpeedCeiling</Name><Type>REAL</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>0</LBound><Elements>4</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ Ceiling per controller operating mode; the CM applies MIN(ceiling, ParCmd.SpeedScale).
 UNKNOWN = 0 so an unreported mode yields the safest ceiling, not the fastest.
 Indexed by E_RobotOpMode's ordinals - UNKNOWN, AUTO_REMOTE,
 MANUAL_REDUCED, MANUAL_HIGH. UNKNOWN is 0.0 on purpose: a mode the
 controller has not reported never earns a speed allowance.]]></Comment><BitSize>128</BitSize><BitOffs>160</BitOffs><Default><SubItem><Name>[0]</Name><Value>0</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[1]</Name><Value>100</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[2]</Name><Value>25</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[3]</Name><Value>100</Value></SubItem></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>DefaultMode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotOpMode</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ v2 - the request half of I.4a(a). DefaultMode is the most restrictive mode
 this cell supports: requested at link-up and whenever a reported mode is
 lost, so a freshly connected controller is never left where somebody asked
 before. UNKNOWN is refused at prepare (it is not a request).]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>288</BitOffs><Default><EnumText>E_RobotOpMode.MANUAL_REDUCED</EnumText></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ModeTimeout</Name><Type>TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ REQUEST_MODE faults when the controller has not granted it by then]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>320</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#10S</DateTime></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>JogTimeout</Name><Type>TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ a held jog stops when the request stops arriving this long (O10)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>352</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#200MS</DateTime></Default></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_RobotParCmd</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Latched by the base on the Execute rising edge (S6.1). No Offset field yet:
 the runtime-correction exception of I.8a is deferred with the connector support
 for it - declaring a field no consumer reads would be dead surface, and an
 unvalidated offset would be worse (S14).]]></Comment><BitSize>256</BitSize><SubItem><Name>TargetId</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ point / list / pallet / tool / frame - or the TO position]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs><Default><Value>0</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>FromId</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ FROM position (MOVE_TEMPLATE only)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs><Default><Value>0</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Nest</Name><Type>DINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ nest index (RUN_PALLET only)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Default><Value>0</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>StartIdx</Name><Type>DINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ sub-path bounds (RUN_PATH; -1,-1 = whole list)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>96</BitOffs><Default><Value>-1</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>EndIdx</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs><Default><Value>-1</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SpeedScale</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ process speed for THIS command, % of taught (I.4a(b))]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>160</BitOffs><Default><Value>100</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>AcknowledgeController</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ RECONNECT also clears the robot's own fault]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>192</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Mode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotOpMode</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ REQUEST_MODE only; UNKNOWN is refused]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>224</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_RobotOutCmd</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Valid on Done (S3.10).]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><SubItem><Name>ReachedId</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ position actually reached]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_RobotUserSignal</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Annex I I.3 - one declared user signal as FB_RobotCM publishes it. Empty Key
 = slot not declared. Data the robot program reads or reports, never a command.]]></Comment><BitSize>832</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Key</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ localization key naming the signal]]></Comment><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ToRobot</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE: the PLC writes it; FALSE: the robot reports it]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>648</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Kind</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotSignalKind</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>672</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Value</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ last written (to robot) or last reported (from robot)]]></Comment><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>704</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Valid</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ FALSE while the link is down: never a stale value as fresh]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>768</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_RobotOutImm</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Cyclic live status mirrored from the connector, plus the first-out diagnostic.]]></Comment><BitSize>7296</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Linked</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Referenced</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>8</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>MotionBusy</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ the ARM is moving - not the command handshake]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>16</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ActualMode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotOpMode</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ what the controller REPORTS (I.4a(a))]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>CurrentArea</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ 0 = none/undefined (I.11)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ProtectiveStop</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ process protection, NOT S9 safety (I.4a(c))]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>96</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Resumable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ resume still valid on the retained path (I.4b)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>104</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SpeedScale</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ scale last sent: MIN(mode ceiling, recipe scale) (I.4a(b))]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>RequestedMode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotOpMode</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ what the PLC last REQUESTED, beside the report (I.4a(a))]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>160</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ArmPowerOn</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ the controller reports its drives powered (I.4)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>192</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>PathIndex</Name><Type>DINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ last completed point of the current/last RUN_PATH; -1 = none]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>224</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SafetyPermit</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ the S9 alias as supplied - read-only status, never a grant]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>256</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Jogging</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ a held jog is driving the arm (S7.6.1)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>264</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>JogStopReason</Name><Type>DINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ why the last jog stopped or was refused; 0 = released]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>288</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>JogMode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotJogMode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>320</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>JogAxis</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>352</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>UserSignals</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_RobotUserSignal</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>8</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ declared slots only (I.3)]]></Comment><BitSize>6656</BitSize><BitOffs>384</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Capabilities</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_RobotCapabilities</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ what the connected controller says it offers (I.3)]]></Comment><BitSize>192</BitSize><BitOffs>7040</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>BrakeTestDue</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ the controller asks for its brake test (also a state flag)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>7232</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SafeReferenceDue</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ the controller asks for its safe reference run (also a state flag)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>7240</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_RobotCM</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Annex I I.4 - the robot Control Module. An ordinary CM: it EXTENDS
 FB_ControlModuleBase and adds only its device logic; the handshake, first-out
 stamping, rollup and publication are base-owned and proven in FB_Base_Tests.

 Its additions over a plain CM are the annex's three device facts plus the
 HELD translation:
   - every command first requires Linked (Annex D), and a refusal is ADOPTED
     verbatim from the connector's LastResult rather than re-classified (S8.2);
   - validate-then-command (S5.6): the speed band, the controller's reported
     mode and the reference state are checked BEFORE anything reaches the floor,
     in that order - a bad parameter is malformed regardless of the mode, and
     a mode problem is more specific than a reference problem;
   - a protective stop aborts with its OWN reason so the alarm record never
     misreports a process event as a safety event (I.4a(c));
   - a lost permissive HOLDS on-path (I.4b): the connector is Interrupted at
     hold onset and Resumed on release, and a release that cannot resume -
     the arm was jogged while held - faults ROBOT_RESUME_INVALID instead of
     driving back through untaught space. HELD, not fault, for the permissive
     itself: that is this repo's settled doctrine (a lost permissive is
     restorable operator/process state, Core S6.1).

 And the rest of I.4a/I.4 the shipped type now carries:
   - the REQUEST half of the operating mode: the configured most restrictive
     mode is requested at link-up and on loss of the report, REQUEST_MODE asks
     for another and completes only when the controller REPORTS it, and the
     request is published beside the report so an ungranted one stays visible;
   - the S9 safety alias (SetSafetyPermit), read-only: losing it drops arm
     power and stops a running command with ROBOT_SAFETY_DROPPED; regaining it
     re-enables nothing (S9.3/S9.4). Kept apart from Intlk on purpose: a lost
     APPLICATION permissive holds on-path, a lost SAFETY alias does not;
   - a held jog (JOG_POS/JOG_NEG), only in a manual mode reported by the
     controller, only with the enabling device held, never while a command runs;
   - the active load case (SET_PAYLOAD), the arm-power fact and path progress
     (PathIndex: an aborted path is continued by a DELIBERATE RUN_PATH from the
     next point, never automatically);
   - a declared user-signal channel - data for the robot program, never a
     command (M_DeclareUserSignal / M_WriteUserSignal, published read-only);
   - the controller's capabilities, published read-only: a command it does not
     offer is refused before anything is sent, jog axes and user signals are
     bounded by what it carries;
   - the controller's own routines: its demands for a brake test and a safe
     reference run published as state flags, BRAKE_TEST / SAFE_REFERENCE to run
     them, passed only when the controller withdraws the demand;
   - no move to a point that was never taught: a point-addressed command without
     a point is refused here, an untaught one by the controller, both with
     ROBOT_POINT_UNKNOWN - never a drive to a default pose;
   - declared one-press manual moves to taught points (M_DeclareManualMove), in
     the static catalog, through every gate a program command meets.]]></Comment><BitSize>317696</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_ControlModuleBase</ExtendsType><SubItem><Name>Command</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotCommand</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>265472</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ParCfg</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_RobotParCfg</Type><BitSize>384</BitSize><BitOffs>265504</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ParCmd</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_RobotParCmd</Type><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>265888</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>OutCmd</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_RobotOutCmd</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>266144</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>OutImm</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_RobotOutImm</Type><BitSize>7296</BitSize><BitOffs>266176</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Intlk</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_PermIntlk</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ conditions are DECLARED BY THE APPLICATION (S7.2)]]></Comment><BitSize>40320</BitSize><BitOffs>273472</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_conn</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">I_RobotConnector</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>313792</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>OPC.UA.DA</Name><Value>0</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_routines</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">I_RobotRoutines</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ the controller's own routines, when the connector offers them (I.5b)]]></Comment><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>313856</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>OPC.UA.DA</Name><Value>0</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_tMove</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>313920</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_heldOnPath</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ an Interrupt is outstanding (I.4b)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>314176</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_appCond</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>16</Elements></ArrayInfo><BitSize>128</BitSize><BitOffs>314184</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_applied</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ the scale last sent: MIN(mode ceiling, recipe scale)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>314336</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_requested</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotOpMode</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ the mode last REQUESTED]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>314368</BitOffs><Default><EnumText>E_RobotOpMode.MANUAL_REDUCED</EnumText></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_wasLinked</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>314400</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_reportSeen</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ a real mode was reported since the link came up]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>314408</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_safetyPermit</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ §9 alias as supplied; FALSE until an application supplies one or simulation is enabled]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>314416</BitOffs><Default><Bool>false</Bool></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_safetyPrev</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>314424</BitOffs><Default><Bool>false</Bool></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_safetyKey</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ names the alias in the fault; '' = the generic text]]></Comment><BitSize>2048</BitSize><BitOffs>314432</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_safetyConfigured</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ SetSafetyPermit was called explicitly]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>316480</BitOffs><Default><Bool>false</Bool></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_simOverride</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ deliberate simulation override (F-02)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>316488</BitOffs><Default><Bool>false</Bool></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_simulated</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ connector queried as I_SimulatedRobotConnector]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>316496</BitOffs><Default><Bool>false</Bool></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_tPowerRetry</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ re-ask for power off while it is still reported on]]></Comment><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>316544</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_jogReqDir</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ direction asked for this scan (RequestHeldCommand)]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>316800</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_jogDir</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ direction the connector was started in]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>316816</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_jogSeen</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>316832</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_jogEnabled</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>316840</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_jogDriving</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>316848</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_tJogStale</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>316864</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_jogMode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotJogMode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>317120</BitOffs><Default><EnumText>E_RobotJogMode.JOINT</EnumText></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_jogAxis</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>317152</BitOffs><Default><Value>1</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_caps</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_RobotCapabilities</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ the connector's report, read once per scan (C0185)]]></Comment><BitSize>192</BitSize><BitOffs>317184</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_movePoint</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>8</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ declared manual moves; 0 = slot free]]></Comment><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>317376</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_manualSlot</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ the declared move this command runs; 0 = not one]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>317632</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>SetJogSelection</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ What a held jog moves: the frame and the axis (1..PL_Robot.MAX_JOG_AXES).
 Chosen by the application (a selector, a pendant-side choice); refused while
 a jog is driving, so the axis never changes under a held button.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Mode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotJogMode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Axis</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_UserSignalCyclic</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Publish the declared signals: the robot's reports for from-robot slots, the
 last write for to-robot slots, and Valid only while the link is up and the
 controller carries the slot.]]></Comment><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_Issue</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ One ID-addressed primitive per command. FALSE = the connector refused.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>_M_AdoptRefusal</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ A connector refusal carries its reason in LastResult (I.3) - adopt it
 VERBATIM (S8.2), never re-classified. A refusal with no reason breaks I.3;
 it is still named, never left as a fault with a zero code.]]></Comment><Local><Name>_cd</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</Type><BitSize>5568</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_WriteUserSignal</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Write a declared to-robot signal. The value must fit its kind - 0 or 1 for a
 flag, a whole number for an integer - and is refused otherwise, never rounded.
 Called by the owning EM; not a command and not an HMI write.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Index</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Value</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>RequestHeldCommand</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §7.6.1 held command - JOG_POS / JOG_NEG, called EVERY SCAN while the operator
 holds the control. It only RECORDS the request; the arm moves from
 _M_JogCyclic, where every gate is weighed in one place (the FB_AxisCM shape).
 A robot jog always needs the enabling device: unlike the axis there is no
 station opt-out, because the arm's reach is the hazard.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Value</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Enable</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ManualEnableStatus</Type><BitSize>664</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>OnCyclic</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Mirror the connector's published facts; the device logic is in _M_Dispatch.]]></Comment><ReturnType>DINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>_c</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</Type><BitSize>5568</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>brakeDue</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>safeRefDue</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>SetCondition</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Drive a condition declared by DeclareCondition, every scan.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Index</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Ok</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_TargetId</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The ID this command addresses: a declared manual move's own point, else
 ParCmd.TargetId.]]></Comment><ReturnType>DWORD</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>_M_ModeKnown</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Mode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotOpMode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_Scale</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The speed this command asks for. A one-press manual move carries no speed of
 its own: it runs at the slowest the cell allows (ParCfg.SpeedScaleMin), the one
 nobody has to justify; the mode ceiling still applies on top.]]></Comment><ReturnType>REAL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>OnAbort</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.14.2 - an aborted command stops the ARM, not only the handshake. The base
 ends the command; this sends the stop (SRCI GroupStop). Without it the module
 reported ABORTED while the robot carried on.]]></Comment><ReturnType>DINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>_M_Tag</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ S8.11.4(a) - name the command being timed, so the record reads as an operation
 rather than an enum ordinal. Labels are catalogue keys, resolved by the HMI.]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>_M_Supported</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The commands _M_Issue sends. RECONNECT and REQUEST_MODE are dispatched
 before it; JOG_* are HELD commands and never arrive through Execute.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Cmd</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotCommand</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_IsMotion</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Commands the controller's mode and reference state must permit. POWER_* and
 SET_* are selection, not motion; HOME is sequenced motion and is included, and
 so are the controller's routines - they move the arm.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Cmd</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotCommand</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>DeclareCondition</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core S7.2.1 - the application names its own conditions on this module; the
 library declares none. For a robot that matters more than usual: the guard,
 the safe-zone acknowledgement and the "cell clear" are all facts only the
 station can see. Declared conditions start FALSE - declaring one states an
 intent to gate, so a half-wired station holds rather than moves.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Index</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>DescriptionKey</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Reason</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Reason</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Bypassable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>OnCommandStart</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ S3.14 one-shot on the accepted Execute edge, before OnCyclic/_M_Dispatch.
 Command-local reset only - the process behaviour stays in dispatch.]]></Comment><ReturnType>DINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>_M_IsAddressed</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Commands that name a point, list or pallet by ID - the ones a never-taught or
 missing ID makes meaningless.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Cmd</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotCommand</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>PrepareRecipe</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §5.6 - a speed band, ceilings, default mode or timeouts this type cannot honour
 are refused here, so they never reach a command as behaviour. This type has no
 recipe provider: ParCfg is the composition root's and is judged as it stands.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Model</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ModelId</Type><BitSize>7856</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>ok</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_IsRoutine</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The controller's own routines: run at its own speed, judged by its own demand.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Cmd</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotCommand</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_Dispatch</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The ONLY thing this type writes (Core S2.2): validation ladder (S5.6), then the
 ID-addressed primitive, then completion/hold/timeout at step 20.]]></Comment><Local><Name>_cd</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ C0185: cannot read .member off a property result]]></Comment><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</Type><BitSize>5568</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>SetSafetyPermit</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §9, read-only - the robot's safety alias as the certified system reports
 it (STO clear, safe zone satisfied, ...), supplied by the application every
 scan like SetAreaSafe. It GRANTS nothing: TRUE only lets ordinary requests
 through. FALSE drops arm power and stops a running command with
 ROBOT_SAFETY_DROPPED; TRUE again re-enables nothing (§9.3/§9.4). Defaults
 FALSE (fail-closed, O10): an un-aliased real robot cannot move unless SetSimulationOverride is set.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Permit</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>DescriptionKey</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ names the alias in the fault; '' = the generic text]]></Comment><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_DeclareUserSignal</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ I.3 user channel - declare one plain signal exchanged with the robot program
 (a gripper flag, a program counter). Bounded by PL_Robot.MAX_USER_SIGNALS and
 published read-only in OutImm.UserSignals, so the generic HMI shows it. DATA,
 never a command: positions, modes, speeds and "go" requests stay on the
 ID-addressed command surface. Refused out of range, for an empty key, an
 unknown kind, or a second declaration of the same slot.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Index</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Key</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ToRobot</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Kind</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotSignalKind</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_JogCyclic</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The one place a jog starts, continues or stops, run every scan whether or not
 anybody asked - "nobody asked" is exactly what must stop it. A jog is started
 once (SRCI GroupJog) and stopped with Abort (GroupStop): the connector is never
 asked to jog every scan.]]></Comment><Local><Name>manual</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>drive</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>_jd</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</Type><BitSize>5568</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_SafetyCyclic</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The safety-alias reaction, every scan. A running command is stopped FIRST
 (the stop must not wait behind anything) and faulted; power is then asked off
 on the falling edge, and again every POWER_RETRY while the controller still
 reports it on. Nothing here ever powers ON.]]></Comment><Local><Name>text</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>POWER_RETRY</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_KindKnown</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Kind</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotSignalKind</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_ApplyConditions</Name><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>Setup</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Wire identity and the connector. Called once from the owning EM/Unit (S3.11).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Name</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Robot</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">I_RobotConnector</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>InitialModel</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ModelId</Type><BitSize>7856</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>simConnector</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">I_SimulatedRobotConnector</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_RequestMode</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ REQUEST_MODE (I.4a(a)): send the request, then wait for the controller to
 REPORT the mode. A request it never grants faults after ModeTimeout and stays
 published as requested beside what is reported - visibly ungranted.]]></Comment><Local><Name>_cd</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</Type><BitSize>5568</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_DeclareManualMove</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Declare a one-press manual move to a TAUGHT point, published in the §7.6.1
 catalog under LabelKey so the generic HMI offers it with no station screen.
 It runs as MOVE_FROM_AREA - the controller resolves the route from wherever
 the arm stands - through every gate a program command meets (the Unit's
 manual release, link, safety alias, AUTO_REMOTE, reference, interlocks), at
 ParCfg.SpeedScaleMin. Declared once, after Setup: the catalog is static
 configuration (§3.10.2). Refused out of range, for point 0, an empty label, a
 second declaration of the same slot, or a full catalog.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Slot</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>PointId</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>LabelKey</Name><Type>STRING(120)</Type><BitSize>968</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_FaultStopped</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Stop the arm, THEN fault. _M_FaultN raises the reason without touching motion,
 so faulting first would leave a moving robot commanded - the same defect
 FB_AxisCM._M_FaultStopped exists to prevent, and no less serious here.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Code</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Text</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>SetSimulationOverride</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Deliberately override safety permit gating for offline simulation or bench testing (Core §10.6, §9.8, F-02).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Enable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_Offered</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Is this command offered? The routines need the I.5b interface on the
 connector. Otherwise bit n of Capabilities.Commands is E_RobotCommand n, and
 not reported = not filtered: before the controller has said, its own refusal
 is the only authority there is.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Value</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ an E_RobotCommand value]]></Comment><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotSimFault</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Annex I I.5c - the failures the simulation connector can be told to inject.
 Bounded and enumerated (O10): the reasons of I.2 are exactly what cannot be
 proven against a real arm without deliberately breaking a cell, so the sim
 must be able to produce them on demand - but only the ones some test or
 commissioning rehearsal actually needs, never a knob per reason.]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BaseType>DINT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>NONE</Text><Enum>0</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>POINT_UNREACHABLE</Text><Enum>1</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ the next motion command is refused before it starts]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>NO_ROUTE</Text><Enum>2</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ the next template move finds no path (I.9)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>LINK_LOSS</Text><Enum>3</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ the heartbeat fails; the base drops and re-backs off]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>PROTECTIVE_STOP</Text><Enum>4</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ the crash device trips, in motion or at rest]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>NOT_RESUMABLE</Text><Enum>5</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ a held move cannot resume - the arm left the path (I.4b)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>MODE_NOT_GRANTED</Text><Enum>6</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ a mode request is accepted but the reported mode never changes (I.4a(a))]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>ROUTINE_FAILED</Text><Enum>7</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ a brake test / safe reference run ends with its demand still standing]]></Comment></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>qualified_only</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_SimRobotConnector</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Annex I I.5c - the SIMULATION connector. O6 requires every module to run
 unchanged against simulated or real I/O; for a robot the seam is the connector,
 not the HAL, so without this type a robot CM cannot be virtually commissioned
 at all and a station containing one cannot be dry-run before the arm arrives.

 It is deliberately NOT a kinematic simulator and does not pretend to be one.
 What it is faithful about is the CONTRACT: the handshake and its timing, the
 facts it publishes about itself, and its refusals. The pose it reports is a
 plausible synthetic interpolation so displays and area checks have something
 real to move on - never a claim about where an actual arm would be.

 Selected as configuration (S2.6): the CM holds I_RobotConnector, so swapping
 this for FB_StaubliVal3Connector changes a declaration and nothing else. That
 is the whole point - simulation is paid once in the connector family, never
 per station (S1.1 O1).]]></Comment><BitSize>22016</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_DeviceConnectorBase</ExtendsType><Implements Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">I_RobotConnector</Implements><Implements Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">I_RobotRoutines</Implements><Implements Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">I_SimulatedRobotConnector</Implements><SubItem><Name>MoveTime</Name><Type>TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ how long an accepted motion takes]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>7616</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#200MS</DateTime></Default><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>HomeTime</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>7648</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#500MS</DateTime></Default><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>HomeArea</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ area reported once homed (I.11)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>7680</BitOffs><Default><Value>1</Value></Default><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Inject</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_RobotSimFault</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ I.5c - level, cleared by the caller]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>7712</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>UserIn</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>8</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ what the robot program reports (I.3)]]></Comment><BitSize>512</BitSize><BitOffs>7744</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Offered</Name><Type>LWORD</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ commands offered: bit n = E_RobotCommand n (1..17)]]></Comment><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>8256</BitOffs><Default><Value>262142</Value></Default><Prop