DATA[ Build a safety facet carrying one enabling device in a given state.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Permitting</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Faulted</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_SeparatorHal</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ HAL view (S10.3). The driver owns invert/debounce and the raw %I/%Q symbols;
 the module only ever touches these clean signals, so simulation and hardware
 are the same code (S2.6).]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><SubItem><Name>CarrierAt</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ input  - carrier present at the separator]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>CarrierAfter</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ input  - carrier present just past the separator]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>8</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>OpenedFb</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ input  - separator-opened feedback (optional)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>16</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ValveOpen</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ output - drives the open solenoid]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>24</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_SeparatorCommand</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Annex A separator/stopper. NONE is the unset value: dispatch rejects it (S5.6).]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BaseType>DINT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>NONE</Text><Enum>0</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>SEPARATE</Text><Enum>1</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ release exactly one carrier]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>OPEN_CLOSE</Text><Enum>2</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ hold the stopper open or closed per ParCmd.OpenStopper]]></Comment></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>qualified_only</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_SeparatorMode</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Separation behaviour variants (Annex A). SEPARATOR checks the carrier at AND
 after the device; STOPPER checks only at it.]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BaseType>DINT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>SEPARATOR</Text><Enum>0</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>STOPPER</Text><Enum>1</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>ASISTOPPER</Text><Enum>2</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>LEADFRAME</Text><Enum>3</Enum></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>qualified_only</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_SeparatorParCfg</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core S3.8: SchemaVersion FIRST, initialized to the expected version.]]></Comment><BitSize>224</BitSize><SubItem><Name>SchemaVersion</Name><Type>UINT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs><Default><Value>1</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Mode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_SeparatorMode</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs><Default><EnumText>E_SeparatorMode.SEPARATOR</EnumText></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>CheckAfter</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ require the carrier-after arrival/clear checks]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Default><Bool>true</Bool></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>UsesOpenFb</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ require the open feedback on OPEN_CLOSE]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>72</BitOffs><Default><Bool>false</Bool></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>MaxOpenTime</Name><Type>TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ CarrierAt must clear within this after opening]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>96</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#3S</DateTime></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SOnMaxTime</Name><Type>TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ CarrierAfter must arrive/clear within this]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#3S</DateTime></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>CloseDelay</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>160</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#0S</DateTime></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Timeout</Name><Type>TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ overall command timeout]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>192</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#10S</DateTime></Default></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_SeparatorParCmd</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Latched by the base on the Execute rising edge (S6.1).]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><SubItem><Name>OpenStopper</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ OPEN_CLOSE: TRUE = open, FALSE = close]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_SeparatorOutCmd</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Valid on Done (S3.12).]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><SubItem><Name>SeparateOk</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SeparatorOpen</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>8</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_SeparatorOutImm</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Cyclic live status plus the first-out diagnostic (S3.12, S6.9).]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><SubItem><Name>CarrierAt</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>CarrierAfter</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>8</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>OpenedFb</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>16</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ValveOpen</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>24</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_SeparatorCM</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Annex A worked example on the base class: the type is ONLY its device logic.

 It defines NO interlocks of its own, deliberately. Core S7.2.1 confines a
 reusable library to "device-intrinsic conditions or explicitly injected generic
 policy", and none of Annex A's four published conditions qualify: area-safe is
 a S9.2 safety alias, air pressure is a utility, jam is a flag that is not even
 on this device's HAL, and downstream-ready is line policy. All four belong to
 the owning Unit's Release/Permissives object (S7.2.1, S4.2).

 So the application declares and drives them through DeclareCondition/
 SetCondition. They land in this module's own FB_PermIntlk, which keeps the
 provenance S7.2.1 requires - first-out, release report and HMI drill-down all
 read the same ST_IntlkCond records - without the library naming policy it
 cannot see. A per-condition setter was rejected: FB_CylinderCM.SetAreaSafe is
 exactly that shape and no application has ever called it.]]></Comment><BitSize>307136</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_ControlModuleBase</ExtendsType><SubItem><Name>Command</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_SeparatorCommand</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>265472</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ParCfg</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_SeparatorParCfg</Type><BitSize>224</BitSize><BitOffs>265504</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ParCmd</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_SeparatorParCmd</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>265728</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>OutCmd</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_SeparatorOutCmd</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>265736</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>OutImm</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_SeparatorOutImm</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>265752</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Intlk</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_PermIntlk</Type><BitSize>40320</BitSize><BitOffs>265792</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_hal</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules" ReferenceTo="true">ST_SeparatorHal</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>306112</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>OPC.UA.DA</Name><Value>0</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_recipe</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_RecipeProvider</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>306176</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>OPC.UA.DA</Name><Value>0</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_tPhase</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ per-phase timeout (open / clear / arrive)]]></Comment><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>306240</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_tClose</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ close delay]]></Comment><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>306496</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_parCfgStaged</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_SeparatorParCfg</Type><BitSize>224</BitSize><BitOffs>306752</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_recipePrepared</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>306976</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_appCond</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>16</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ Application-owned conditions (S7.2.1). Declared FALSE so a declared-but-
 undriven condition holds the module rather than silently permitting it.]]></Comment><BitSize>128</BitSize><BitOffs>306984</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>CommitRecipe</Name></Method><Method><Name>WithdrawOutputs</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Functional stop used by an owning sequence on abort/interlock loss.
 This is not a certified stop; the safety system remains authoritative (S9).]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>OnAbort</Name><ReturnType>DINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>_M_OpenClose</Name></Method><Method><Name>_M_ApplyConditions</Name><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>Setup</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Name</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>HalRef</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules" ReferenceTo="true">ST_SeparatorHal</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Recipe</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_RecipeProvider</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>InitialModel</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ModelId</Type><BitSize>7856</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>SetCondition</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Drive a condition declared by DeclareCondition. Call it every scan from the
 owning Unit's Release object; the value is re-applied in OnCyclic so dispatch
 and the release report always read the same state.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Index</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Ok</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>AbortRecipe</Name></Method><Method><Name>DeclareCondition</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core S7.2.1 - the application names its own conditions on this module.
 The library defines none, so every index is the application's to claim.
 Returns FALSE on an out-of-range index rather than silently ignoring it (S5.6).

 Declared conditions start FALSE: declaring one states an intent to gate, so
 the fail-closed default is to hold until the application drives it. A station
 that wants no gate simply declares nothing.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Index</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>DescriptionKey</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Reason</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Reason</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Bypassable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_Dispatch</Name><Local><Name>dg</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</Type><BitSize>5568</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>OnCyclic</Name><ReturnType>DINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>PrepareRecipe</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Model</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ModelId</Type><BitSize>7856</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_FaultClosed</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Withdraw the valve, THEN fault. _M_FaultN only raises the reason; it does not
 touch outputs, so faulting from an open phase would leave the stopper
 energised while the module reported ERROR. Annex A faults and closes in one
 step for exactly this reason, and a separator that stays open on a fault
 keeps releasing carriers it can no longer account for.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Code</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Text</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_Separator_Tests</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Annex A separator/stopper. T1/T4 are proven once in FB_Base_Tests for every
 inheriting type and are deliberately NOT repeated here (Core S5.7).

 The first test is the one that matters most: this type declares NO interlocks
 of its own (S7.2.1), so the suite proves both halves of that contract - nothing
 gates a station that declares nothing, and a condition the application declares
 is fail-closed until the application drives it.]]></Comment><BitSize>35418176</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="TcUnit">FB_TestSuite</ExtendsType><SubItem><Name>_hal</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_SeparatorHal</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>33574912</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_sep</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_SeparatorCM</Type><BitSize>307136</BitSize><BitOffs>33574976</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_halT3</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_SeparatorHal</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>33882112</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_sepT3</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_SeparatorCM</Type><BitSize>307136</BitSize><BitOffs>33882176</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_halSep</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_SeparatorHal</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>34189312</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_sepSep</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_SeparatorCM</Type><BitSize>307136</BitSize><BitOffs>34189376</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_halNo</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_SeparatorHal</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>34496512</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_sepNo</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_SeparatorCM</Type><BitSize>307136</BitSize><BitOffs>34496576</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_halOc</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_SeparatorHal</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>34803712</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_sepOc</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_SeparatorCM</Type><BitSize>307136</BitSize><BitOffs>34803776</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_halBad</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_SeparatorHal</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>35110912</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_sepBad</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_SeparatorCM</Type><BitSize>307136</BitSize><BitOffs>35110976</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>35418112</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_w1</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>35418128</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_w2</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>35418136</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_w3</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>35418144</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_w4</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>35418152</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_w5</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>35418160</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_w6</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>35418168</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>Library_declares_no_interlocks_and_application_conditions_are_fail_closed</Name></Method><Method><Name>Separate_releases_one_carrier_and_completes</Name></Method><Method><Name>Interlock_withholds_the_valve_and_holds_rather_than_faults</Name></Method><Method><Name>Open_close_confirms_feedback_only_when_configured</Name></Method><Method><Name>No_carrier_at_the_separator_faults_10001</Name></Method><Method><Name>Unsupported_command_is_rejected</Name></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_Engineering_Tests</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §7.5 under test: the gate register is write-once and build-driven, the
 standing §7.5.2 annunciation is LOW/SYSTEM/AUTO_RESET, no operator action
 closes it, and §10.5.1 forcing is refused unless the register arms it.

 The assertions about OUTPUT_FORCING are written against
 PL_FraktalEngineering.OUTPUT_FORCING rather than against TRUE or FALSE, so the
 suite is green in BOTH images and proves the two are actually coupled - a test
 hard-coded to the production value would pass while the commissioning build
 silently armed nothing.]]></Comment><BitSize>36398656</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="TcUnit">FB_TestSuite</ExtendsType><SubItem><Name>_mode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_EngineeringMode</Type><BitSize>15616</BitSize><BitOffs>33574912</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_overflow</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_EngineeringMode</Type><BitSize>15616</BitSize><BitOffs>33590528</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_u</Name><Type>FB_ProbeUnit</Type><BitSize>2776768</BitSize><BitOffs>33606144</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_gateMode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_EngineeringMode</Type><BitSize>15616</BitSize><BitOffs>36382912</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>36398528</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_slot</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>36398544</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_second</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>36398560</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_w1</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>36398576</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_w2</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>36398584</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_w3</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>36398592</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_w4</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>36398600</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>Inactive_gate_is_not_registered_and_declaring_is_idempotent</Name></Method><Method><Name>Register_overflow_is_reported_not_silent</Name><Local><Name>gateName</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>Forcing_is_armed_only_by_the_build_constant</Name></Method><Method><Name>Active_gate_annunciates_low_system_and_no_reset_closes_it</Name></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_ProbeConfigCM</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b probe: a leaf module that declares one editable value of each storage
 class, so the registry can be tested where it actually lives — on a child,
 reached by the root's recursive walk rather than by the root's own handler.
 Values are plain VAR_INPUT here (configuration data, per the transport
 contract): this suite proves registration, validation and routing, while
 retention is TwinCAT's job and is not what these tests assert.]]></Comment><BitSize>268352</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_ControlModuleBase</ExtendsType><SubItem><Name>SettleTime</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>265472</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#500MS</DateTime></Default><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Retries</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>265504</BitOffs><Default><Value>3</Value></Default><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Enabled</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>265536</BitOffs><Default><Bool>true</Bool></Default><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Label</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>265544</BitOffs><Default><String>default</String></Default><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Mode</Name><Type>DINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ an enumeration stored as its ordinal]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>266208</BitOffs><Default><Value>1</Value></Default><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>RefuseText</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Test seam for the module-invariant hook: the one candidate this module
 refuses whatever its type and range say.]]></Comment><BitSize>2048</BitSize><BitOffs>266240</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>RefusedCount</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ proves the hook ran, not just that a write failed]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>268288</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><Method><Name>Setup</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Name</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_Dispatch</Name></Method><Method><Name>_M_OnConfigWrite</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.10.2 — the module-specific invariant hook. Refuses one candidate outright
 so the suite can prove a hook rejection leaves the value untouched, exactly
 like a range rejection does.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>WriteKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>TextValue</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_ProbeConfigUnit</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b probe root: one own editable value plus one child that owns three more.
 The point of the pair is the walk — the root registers no routing code at all,
 so a test that writes a child's value proves the generic path rather than a
 hand-written override (§1.1 O1).]]></Comment><BitSize>3044928</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_UnitBase</ExtendsType><SubItem><Name>Child</Name><Type>FB_ProbeConfigCM</Type><BitSize>268352</BitSize><BitOffs>2776512</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>CycleLimit</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>3044864</BitOffs><Default><Value>100</Value></Default><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><Method><Name>Setup</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Name</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_Dispatch</Name></Method><Method><Name>M_SetChildRefuse</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Test seam. The child is reachable from outside for READING, but a nested FB
 behind an output is not an assignment target, so the owner sets it — which is
 also how a real composite would configure its own child.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Text</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_ConfigWrite_Tests</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §3.8b/§3.10.2 under test: a module declares its own editable values, the
 root's walk publishes them as complete capabilities and carries writes back to
 the owner, and everything the owner did not agree to is refused without
 changing a byte. The pair FB_ProbeConfigUnit/FB_ProbeConfigCM deliberately
 contains no routing code — if these pass, a new module type needs none either.]]></Comment><BitSize>37098944</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="TcUnit">FB_TestSuite</ExtendsType><SubItem><Name>_u</Name><Type>FB_ProbeConfigUnit</Type><BitSize>3044928</BitSize><BitOffs>33574912</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_init</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>36619840</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_setupOk</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>36619848</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_pager</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_ConfigPager</Type><BitSize>512</BitSize><BitOffs>36619904</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_page</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigPage</Type><BitSize>197760</BitSize><BitOffs>36620416</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_found</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigEntry</Type><BitSize>12352</BitSize><BitOffs>36818176</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_dup</Name><Type>FB_ProbeConfigCM</Type><BitSize>268352</BitSize><BitOffs>36830528</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_dupOk</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>37098880</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>Module_invariant_hook_can_refuse</Name></Method><Method><Name>Duplicate_key_is_refused_and_the_first_stands</Name></Method><Method><Name>_M_Arm</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ One-time setup, on the first test to run rather than in a constructor: the
 suite's own Setup return value is itself an assertion below.]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>Units_and_choices_publish_codes_and_labels</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core 0.14: a unit is a CODE the HMI translates (the text is derived from it
