 real TwinCAT file service, in the real Boot directory of the runtime.

 The provider keeps its default medium: a file medium in the Boot directory,
 '<key>.a' and '<key>.b' (FB_FilePersistMedium; the medium itself is covered by
 FB_PersistMedium_Tests). A "restart" here is a second provider instance over
 the same retained files - exactly what a cold start, a download or a power
 cycle leaves a new run with. Each test uses its own per-run key, so tests run
 side by side and a previous run's files or confirmation marker can never decide
 this run's result; every test removes its files when it finishes. A real
 runtime restart with the same instance (the confirmation marker) is accepted
 separately.]]></Comment><BitSize>45340352</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="TcUnit">FB_TestSuite</ExtendsType><SubItem><Name>_tag</Name><Type>STRING(24)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ per-run suffix of every key]]></Comment><BitSize>200</BitSize><BitOffs>33574912</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_garbage</Name><Type>BYTE</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>0</LBound><Elements>16</Elements></ArrayInfo><BitSize>128</BitSize><BitOffs>33575112</BitOffs><Default><SubItem><Name>[0]</Name><Value>90</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[1]</Name><Value>90</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[2]</Name><Value>90</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[3]</Name><Value>90</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[4]</Name><Value>90</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[5]</Name><Value>90</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[6]</Name><Value>90</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[7]</Name><Value>90</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[8]</Name><Value>90</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[9]</Name><Value>90</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[10]</Name><Value>90</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[11]</Name><Value>90</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[12]</Name><Value>90</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[13]</Name><Value>90</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[14]</Name><Value>90</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[15]</Name><Value>90</Value></SubItem></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_s1</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>33575248</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_t1</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>33575296</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_p1a</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_LocalAccessProvider</Type><BitSize>52480</BitSize><BitOffs>33575552</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_p1b</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_LocalAccessProvider</Type><BitSize>52480</BitSize><BitOffs>33628032</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_p1c</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_LocalAccessProvider</Type><BitSize>52480</BitSize><BitOffs>33680512</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_f1</Name><Type>