BitSize>52480</BitSize><BitOffs>42333504</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_p4b</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_LocalAccessProvider</Type><BitSize>52480</BitSize><BitOffs>42385984</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_p4c</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_LocalAccessProvider</Type><BitSize>52480</BitSize><BitOffs>42438464</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_f4</Name><Type>FB_ProbeFileOps</Type><BitSize>19776</BitSize><BitOffs>42490944</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_u5</Name><Type>FB_ProbeUnit</Type><BitSize>2776768</BitSize><BitOffs>42510720</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_store5</Name><Type>FB_ProbeAccessStore</Type><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>45287488</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_done5</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ state-changing: runs exactly once]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>45287744</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_p6</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_LocalAccessProvider</Type><BitSize>52480</BitSize><BitOffs>45287808</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_done6</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ state-changing: runs exactly once]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>45340288</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>TEST_TIMEOUT</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>45340320</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#40S</DateTime></Default></SubItem><Method><Name>_M_Stem</Name><ReturnType>STRING(80)</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>648</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Name</Name><Type>STRING(40)</Type><BitSize>328</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_File</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The retained file of one slot, as the file medium names it ('<key>.a').]]></Comment><ReturnType>STRING(255)</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>2048</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Name</Name><Type>STRING(40)</Type><BitSize>328</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>SlotB</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>A_root_announces_a_failed_save_and_a_lost_table_once</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The root's side of a retained table, with the store's outcomes forced: a write
 that cannot be made durable is CONFIG_PERSIST_FAILED until a later one succeeds,
 and a lost table reaches the root's §3.8b restore annunciation exactly once.
 (The provider's own failing write is accepted live, against a real Boot folder.)]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>A_torn_newest_image_falls_back_to_the_previous_one</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ A write interrupted mid-file leaves the other slot intact: the restore takes the
 newest image that validates and never mixes records from the two.]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>A_corrupt_table_is_announced_once_and_replaced</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Both slots unreadable: the loss is reported, nothing half-restored, and what
 survived is written back so the NEXT restart is silent and complete.]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>A_root_restores_logs_in_and_out_and_announces_a_lost_table</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The surface a station uses: nothing but Access.Setup. The root's access manager
 drives the store, a restored user logs in and out through the data-driven
 request, and a lost table is announced through the root's §3.8b path.]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>A_retained_table_survives_a_restart_and_follows_changes</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Restart retention, a PIN change and a level change all come back from storage.]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>Storage_names_are_bounded_and_fixed_before_restore</Name></Method><Method><Name>_M_LevelOf</Name><ReturnType>DINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Provider</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_AccessProvider</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>User</Name><Type>STRING(32)</Type><BitSize>264</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Pin</Name><Type>STRING(32)</Type><BitSize>264</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core.Tc3_IPCDiag">E_IPCDiag_ParameterKey</Name><BitSize>64</BitSize><BaseType>LWORD</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>Unselected</Text><Enum>0</Enum><Properties><Property><Name>conditionalshow</Name></Property></Properties></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>IPCDeviceName</Text><Enum>30399297753710592</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ IPC device name, STRING, read/write (MDP general area)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>IPCHardwareVersion</Text><Enum>7881299616923648</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ IPC hardware version, STRING, constant (MDP general area)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>IPCImageVersion</Text><Enum>7881299616989184</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ IPC image version, STRING, constant (MDP general area)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>IPCVendor</Text><Enum>6473924734353409</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ IPC vendor, UDINT, constant (MDP general area)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>IPCSerialNumber</Text><Enum>12384903168524288</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ serial number (or BTN) of Beckhoff IPC, STRING, read-only (MDP device area)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>IPCBeckhoffIdentificationCod