pace="Fraktal_Core.Tc2_EtherCAT">FB_EcGetSlaveCount</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize><BitOffs>2048</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>conditionalshow</Name></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>RisingEdge</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">R_TRIG</Type><BitSize>128</BitSize><BitOffs>4096</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>conditionalshow</Name></Property></Properties></SubItem><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property><Property><Name>conditionalshow_all_locals</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_EcBusHealth</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §10.5.1 infrastructure service: read the REAL, live state of every
 EtherCAT slave directly from the fieldbus master (Tc2_EtherCAT) and publish it
 per node, so the HMI fieldbus tree mirrors XAE — independent of any Control-On
 or safety verdict. Auto-detects from hardware: the project supplies only the
 master AmsNetId ('' = local CPU) and how its topology node indices line up
 with the master's slave ordering (one offset), not per-node wiring.

 This is not a module tier and owns no process image. It calls
 FB_IoTopologyPublisher.M_SetNodeState for each mapped node.]]></Comment><BitSize>32768</BitSize><SubItem><Name>_pub</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" PointerTo="1">FB_IoTopologyPublisher</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>OPC.UA.DA</Name><Value>0</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_netId</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_System">T_AmsNetID</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ EtherCAT MASTER device AmsNetId (see Setup)]]></Comment><BitSize>192</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_firstSlaveNode</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ topology node index of master slave #1]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>320</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_slaveCount</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ how many slaves the master is asked about]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>336</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_masterNode</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ topology node index of the master itself (0 = none)]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>352</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_attached</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>368</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_slaveNode</Name><Type>INT</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>64</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ §10.5.1 — which topology node each MASTER SLAVE INDEX belongs to.
 _slaveNode[i] = topology node of the master's slave i (0 = unmapped).

 The master enumerates only devices with an EtherCAT slave controller on
 the process-data ring. A bus coupler (EK1200) and a passive end cap
 (EL9011) are in the project tree and in the catalog, but the master never
 lists them -- so "catalog position" and "master slave index" are NOT the
 same sequence. Assuming they were shifted every state by one: the press
 bench published the EL1809's state onto the coupler, the EL2809's onto the
 EL1809, the EL6001's onto the EL2809, and left the real EL6001 and the end
 cap reading OFFLINE while all three cards were in OP. A wrong state on the
 right node is worse than no state: it is a plausible lie.

 Setup's FirstSlaveNode/SlaveCount form still works and fills this map
 consecutively -- correct whenever every catalogued node really is a slave.]]></Comment><BitSize>1024</BitSize><BitOffs>384</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_passiveNode</Name><Type>INT</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>64</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ Topology nodes that are catalogued but are NOT on the master's slave list
 (couplers, end caps). Their state is inferred, never invented: they carry
 the bus and are reachable exactly when the slaves behind them answer.]]></Comment><BitSize>1024</BitSize><BitOffs>1408</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_passiveCount</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>2432</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_fbLocalNetId</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Utilities">FB_GetLocalAmsNetId</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Auto-detection of the EtherCAT master's AmsNetId (no project wiring): the
 master's NetId is the local AMS NetId with the last two bytes replaced by
 2.1 (Beckhoff convention -- a PC 'a.b.c.d.1.1' has its EtherCAT master at
 'a.b.c.d.2.1'; the InfoSys FB_EcGetAllSlaveStates example uses exactly this
 pairing). Overridable via Setup for non-standard configurations.]]></Comment><BitSize>11584</BitSize><BitOffs>2496</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>OPC.UA.DA</Name><Value>0</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_autoDetect</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE = derive the master NetId at runtime]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>14080</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_netIdArr</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_System">T_AmsNetIdArr</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ scratch for the derived master NetId]]></Comment><BitSize>48</BitSize><BitOffs>14088</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>OPC.UA.DA</Name><Value>0</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_fbStates</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core.Tc2_EtherCAT">FB_EcGetAllSlaveStates</Type><BitSize>4224</BitSize><BitOffs>14144</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>OPC.UA.DA</Name><Value>0</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_stateBuf</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core.Tc2_EtherCAT">ST_EcSlaveState</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>0</LBound><Elements>65</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ Bounded state buffer, one ST_EcSlaveState (deviceState + linkState) per
 slave. Beckhoff declares pStateBuf as ARRAY[0..EC_MAX_SLAVES], so this
 buffer is ZERO-BASED: slave i (1..n, master scan order) is _stateBuf[i-1].]]></Comment><BitSize>1040</BitSize><BitOffs>18368</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>OPC.UA.DA</Name><Value>0</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_step</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>19408</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_tPoll</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>19456</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_scanRequested</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Demand gating (§10.5.1 diagnostic surface): only scan while a consumer
 asks. _firstScanDone lets one scan run after Setup so M_BusOk() — which
 feeds control logic, not a view — is never based on unread hardware.]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>19712</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_firstScanDone</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>19720</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_fbDevState</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core.Tc2_EtherCAT">FB_EcGetMasterDevState</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ §8.12/§10.5 master health. Unlike the per-slave picture it is NOT
 demand-gated: alarms and M_BusOk consume it every scan, so it is sampled
 once a second whether or not anyone has the bus view open.]]></Comment><BitSize>2048</BitSize><BitOffs>19776</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>OPC.UA.DA</Name><Value>0</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_fbFrames</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core.Tc2_EtherCAT">FB_EcMasterFrameStatistic</Type><BitSize>3008</BitSize><BitOffs>21824</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>OPC.UA.DA</Name><Value>0</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_fbCrc</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core.Tc2_EtherCAT">FB_EcGetAllSlaveCrcErrors</Type><BitSize>4224</BitSize><BitOffs>24832</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>OPC.UA.DA</Name><Value>0</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_crcBuf</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>0</LBound><Elements>65</Elements></ArrayInfo><BitSize>2080</BitSize><BitOffs>29056</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>OPC.UA.DA</Name><Value>0</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_mPhase</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>31136</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_mPoll</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>31168</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_mSampled</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>31424</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_mSampledAt</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>31456</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_mBaselined</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>31488</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_mWindowStart</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>31520</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_mLostBase</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>31552</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_mCrcBase</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>31584</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_mLastWindowLost</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>31616</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_mLastWindowCrc</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>31648</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>MASTER_FAULT_BITS</Name><Type>WORD</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Tc2_EtherCAT master device-state bits (F_ConvMasterDevStateToString): link
 error 0x0001, I/O locked 0x0002, out of send resources 0x0010, watchdog
 0x0020, driver missing 0x0040, I/O reset 0x0080, a device in INIT/PRE-OP/
 SAFE-OP 0x0100/0x0200/0x0400, a device in error 0x0800. The redundancy-only
 bits 0x0004/0x0008 are not faults of a working line; DC is reported apart.]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>31680</BitOffs><Default><Value>4083</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>MASTER_DC_NOT_IN_SYNC</Name><Type>WORD</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>31696</BitOffs><Default><Value>4096</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>MASTER_POLL</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>31712</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#1S</DateTime></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>MASTER_WINDOW</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>31744</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#10S</DateTime></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>MASTER_FRESH_FOR</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>31776</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#3S</DateTime></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ReadOk</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ last slave-state read succeeded]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>31808</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>LastErrorId</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ ADS error of the last failed read (0 = none)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>31840</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SlavesReported</Name><Type>UINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ slaves the master reports (nSlaves output)]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>31872</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>NetIdMissing</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE = InfoData.AmsNetId not linked (all zero)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>31888</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>MasterNetId</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_System">T_AmsNetID</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ the resolved master NetId actually being used]]></Comment><BitSize>192</BitSize><BitOffs>31896</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>CountMismatch</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE = the master reports a different slave count than the project
 topology declares (missing/extra hardware, or a config not activated).
 §10.5.1: an unmatched mapping is a commissioning error, never guessed.]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>32088</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>DiagRawDeviceState</Name><Type>BYTE</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>8</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ deviceState byte, as received]]></Comment><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>32096</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>DiagRawLinkState</Name><Type>BYTE</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>8</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ linkState byte, as received]]></Comment><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>32160</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>DiagDecodedState</Name><Type>INT</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>8</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ E_NodeState after decoding]]></Comment><BitSize>128</BitSize><BitOffs>32224</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>DiagNodeIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>8</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ topology node each slave maps to]]></Comment><BitSize>128</BitSize><BitOffs>32352</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>DiagBufferBytes</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ cbBufLen passed to the FB]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>32480</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>DiagEntrySize</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ SIZEOF(ST_EcSlaveState)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>32512</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>DiagScanCount</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ completed reads (proves polling)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>32544</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>DiagScanRequested</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ the §10.5.1 demand-gate state]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>32576</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>DiagFirstScanDone</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>32584</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>MasterAvailable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ state, frame and CRC counters read within 3 s]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>32592</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>MasterDevState</Name><Type>WORD</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ raw master device state (F_ConvMasterDevStateToString)]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>32608</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>MasterHealthy</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ available and no MASTER_FAULT_BITS set]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>32624</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>LostFrameCount</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ lost cyclic+queued frames: current or last 10 s window]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>32640</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SlaveErrorCount</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ summed slave CRC errors: current or last 10 s window]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>32672</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>DcSynchronized</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ available and DC not reported out of sync]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>32704</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>MasterErrorId</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ ADS error of the last failed master read (0 = none)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>32736</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><Method><Name>M_MapSlaveNode</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §10.5.1 — state explicitly which topology node the master's slave [SlaveIndex]
 is, for a bus whose catalog is NOT one-to-one with the master's slave list.

 The master enumerates only devices with an EtherCAT slave controller on the
 process-data ring. A bus coupler or a passive end cap appears in the project
 tree and in the catalog, but never in that list, so the default consecutive
 mapping shifts every state onto its neighbour. Call this once per real slave,
 after Setup, and the shift is impossible:

   _busHealth.Setup(..., FirstSlaveNode := 2, SlaveCount := 3, MasterNodeIndex := 1);
   _busHealth.M_MapSlaveNode(SlaveIndex := 1, NodeIndex := 3);  // EL1809
   _busHealth.M_MapSlaveNode(SlaveIndex := 2, NodeIndex := 4);  // EL2809
   _busHealth.M_MapSlaveNode(SlaveIndex := 3, NodeIndex := 5);  // EL6001
   _busHealth.M_MapPassiveNode(NodeIndex := 2);                 // EK1200 coupler
   _busHealth.M_MapPassiveNode(NodeIndex := 6);                 // EL9011 end cap]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>SlaveIndex</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ 1-based index in the master's slave list]]></Comment><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>NodeIndex</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ topology node this slave IS (0 clears the mapping)]]></Comment><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_MapSlaveState</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Decode an ST_EcSlaveState.deviceState byte (Beckhoff Tc2_EtherCAT, EtherCAT
 AL state machine) into the neutral E_NodeState the HMI renders.
   low nibble  = AL state: INIT=1, PREOP=2, BOOTSTRAP=3, SAFEOP=4, OP=8
   high nibble = flags:    ERROR=0x10, INVALID_VPRS=0x20, INITCMD_ERROR=0x40,
                           DISABLED=0x80  -> any set is a fault.
 Source: infosys.beckhoff.com ST_EcSlaveState / EC_DEVICE_STATE_*.]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_NodeState</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>DeviceState</Name><Type>BYTE</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_RequestScan</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §10.5.1 demand gate. Call every cycle with Active := TRUE while a consumer is
 reading the bus picture (the HMI fieldbus view is open, or a mailbox scan was
 requested); FALSE parks the scanner. Held states are NOT invalidated on
 release — a stale-but-true picture beats a fabricated one; the view re-reads
 on its next activation.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Active</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_ApplyMasterSample</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Record one complete master sample; _M_SampleMaster calls it after reading the
 device state, frame statistics and slave CRC counters, and it is the seam a
 fixture drives. The master's counters are cumulative, so each published count
 is the larger of the current window's and the last full window's increase: a
 burst is held for a whole window and a startup's losses never count.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Ok</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ every read of this sample succeeded]]></Comment><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>DevState</Name><Type>WORD</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>LostFrames</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ cumulative lost cyclic + queued frames]]></Comment><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>CrcErrors</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ cumulative slave CRC errors, summed over slaves]]></Comment><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>MonoNow</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>lostNow</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>crcNow</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_PublishMaster</Name><Parameter><Name>MonoNow</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_Refresh</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Non-blocking cyclic refresh: (re)issue the slave-state read at a bounded rate,
 then publish each node's real state. On a read error every mapped node is
 marked OFFLINE (fail-visible: an unreachable master is not "operational").]]></Comment><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>node</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>mapped</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_NodeState</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>linkOk</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>reported</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ slaves the master actually returned this read]]></Comment><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_SampleMaster</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ One bounded ADS read at a time: device state, frame statistics, then the slave
 CRC counters; a sample counts only when all three succeeded.]]></Comment><Local><Name>crc</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>n</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_PublishAllOffline</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Fail-visible fallback: publish every mapped node (and the master) as OFFLINE.
 Used when the master cannot be reached and when its AmsNetId cannot be
 resolved -- an unknown bus must never look "operational" on the HMI.]]></Comment><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>node</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>Setup</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Bind the publisher and describe how topology nodes map to master slaves.
 MasterNetIdArr = OPTIONAL override for the EtherCAT master's AmsNetId. Pass all
   zeros (the normal case, e.g. an unassigned T_AmsNetIdArr) to AUTO-DETECT it at
   runtime: the library reads the local AMS NetId and applies the Beckhoff master
   convention (last two bytes -> 2.1), so no project wiring, no XAE checkbox and
   no hand-typed address are needed. Supply a value only for a non-standard
   configuration (e.g. a remote master, or several masters on one PC), typically
   by linking that master's InfoData.AmsNetId.
 FirstSlaveNode = topology index of the first EtherCAT slave (the coupler);
 SlaveCount = number of consecutive topology nodes that are real slaves, in
 master scan order; MasterNodeIndex = topology index of the EtherCAT master
 itself, or 0 if not represented.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Publisher</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">FB_IoTopologyPublisher</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>MasterNetIdArr</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_System">T_AmsNetIdArr</Type><BitSize>48</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>FirstSlaveNode</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>SlaveCount</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>MasterNodeIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>anyNonZero</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_BusOk</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE when the fieldbus is delivering a valid process image: the master read
 succeeded and every slave THE MASTER REPORTS is OPERATIONAL. This is the
 library-detected replacement for a project-declared "bus valid" flag —
 projects no longer wire their own RealBusOk. Derived from the last M_Refresh
 cycle (no extra I/O).

 A catalog that declares MORE nodes than are fitted does not make this FALSE:
 per N54 D2 the criterion is that the running bus is functioning properly, and
 a stale catalog is a commissioning issue reported through CountMismatch /
 MappingValid (§10.5.1). Conflating the two silently blocks Control On.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>reported</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ slaves the master actually returned]]></Comment><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_MapPassiveNode</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §10.5.1 — declare a catalogued node that carries the bus but is NOT a slave
 the master enumerates (bus coupler, end cap, power feed).

 Its state is INFERRED, never invented: the devices behind it can only answer
 if it is passing traffic, so it is OPERATIONAL exactly when the read
 succeeded and at least one real slave reported. Without this it would sit at
 OFFLINE forever on a perfectly healthy bus -- which is the same "plausible
 lie" the positional mapping produced, just in the other direction.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>NodeIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_TcSystemHealthProbe</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ TC3 §2.3/§2.7/§8.12 adapter. Task timing is measured here from TwinCAT's
