tem><Name Static="true">AccessPersistenceTests</Name><Type>FB_AccessPersistence_Tests</Type><BitSize>45340352</BitSize></SubItem><SubItem><Name Static="true">PlatformHealthTests</Name><Type>FB_PlatformHealth_Tests</Type><BitSize>34972608</BitSize></SubItem><SubItem><Name Static="true">PersistMediumTests</Name><Type>FB_PersistMedium_Tests</Type><BitSize>34972224</BitSize></SubItem><SubItem><Name Static="true">LiveConfigTests</Name><Type>FB_LiveConfig_Tests</Type><BitSize>47813568</BitSize></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name>PRG_PlatformAcceptance</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Live acceptance harness on the ISOLATED test runtime - not a TcUnit suite. After
 the suites finish it keeps running, so an operator can read, over ADS, what the
 real target providers report while they change the target underneath them:
 stop/start the Windows clock observer or Windows Time, corrupt its record, and
 see the Device Manager and EtherCAT master answer (or, on a host without them,
 stay explicitly unavailable). It writes no global: GVL_FraktalTime stays the
 suites' to set. CLOCK_FILE is a dedicated acceptance path, never the
 installed observer's protected default directory.

 Retention is wired as the press wires it (§3.8b, IMPLEMENTATION_NOTES §163): one
 file medium in DATA_FOLDER holds the user table (AccessUsers, key
 'Acceptance.users'), LiveUnit's station and model documents, and LiveSets'
 parameter sets. The same instances, their confirmation markers and their files
 are the only way to accept retention across a real runtime restart or download.
 The acceptance script registers test users by writing RegisterUser/Pin/Level and
 logs in through AccessUnit.Access exactly as an HMI does; it edits LiveUnit's
 values through SetLimit/SetModelSpeed/SaveSet, which call the root's own write
 methods.]]></Comment><SubItem><Name Static="true">_setup</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></SubItem><SubItem><Name Static="true">SaveSet</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></SubItem><SubItem><Name Static="true">LastWriteOk</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></SubItem><SubItem><Name Static="true">_fileOpBusy</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></SubItem><SubItem><Name Static="true">Clock</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_TcWindowsTime</Type><BitSize>8448</BitSize></SubItem><SubItem><Name Static="true">Ipc</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_TcIpcDiagnostics</Type><BitSize>69120</BitSize></SubItem><SubItem><Name Static="true">Bus</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_EcBusHealth</Type><BitSize>32768</BitSize></SubItem><SubItem><Name Static="true">_topology</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_IoTopologyPublisher</Type><BitSize>192</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>OPC.UA.DA</Name><Value>0</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name Static="true">_noMaster</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_System">T_AmsNetIdArr</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ all zero: derive the local master's NetId]]></Comment><BitSize>48</BitSize></SubItem><SubItem><Name Static="true">AccessUnit</Name><Type>FB_ProbeUnit</Type><BitSize>2776768</BitSize></SubItem><SubItem><Name Static="true">AccessUsers</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_LocalAccessProvider</Type><BitSize>52480</BitSize></SubItem><SubItem><Name Static="true">RegisterUser</Name><Type>STRING(32)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ written by the acceptance script, consumed here]]></Comment><BitSize>264</BitSize></SubItem><SubItem><Name Static="true">RegisterPin</Name><Type>STRING(32)</Type><BitSize>264</BitSize></SubItem><SubItem><Name Static="true">RegisterLevel</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_AccessLevel</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></SubItem><SubItem><Name Static="true">Registered</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ accepted registrations this run]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSiz