       thus that all assertions under it should be ignored as well. A test can be ignored either
       because the user has requested so, or because the test is a duplicate name ]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BaseType>BOOL</BaseType><Properties><Property><Name>TcVarGlobal</Name></Property></Properties><BitOffs>633211856</BitOffs></Symbol><Symbol><Name>PL_FraktalEngineering.OUTPUT_FORCING</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §10.5.1 rule 1 — may this image force fieldbus OUTPUT channels from
 the HMI at all? FALSE keeps Forceable FALSE on every channel, so the HMI
 renders no force affordance whatsoever (§3.9), and FB_UnitBase.ForceChannel
 refuses every request before the resolver is ever reached.

 Forcing an INPUT is not offered by this surface in either build (§10.5.1
 rule 2): lying to the logic to bypass a sensor or an interlock is an
 engineering-tool act under separate authority, never an operating practice.]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BaseType>BOOL</BaseType><Default><Bool>false</Bool></Default><Properties><Property><Name>TcVarGlobal</Name></Property></Properties><BitOffs>633211864</BitOffs></Symbol><Symbol><Name>GVL_TcUnit.NumberOfInitializedTestSuites</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The assert function block instance should be 1:1 mapped to
