 not a real machine: a station chain of a hundred-odd steps is ordinary, and the
 overflow is SILENT (the row is dropped, the chart just stops growing).

 The cost is per Unit and it is nearly all strings: one row is ~1.16 kB, of which
 98% is the five localization-key and path fields. 128 rows is ~145 kB of PLC
 memory per Unit and 2176 OPC UA nodes, which is why SequenceSteps is an
 ON-DEMAND subtree on the HMI side (read while the Sequence tab is open, never in
 the cyclic snapshot) - see Specification/HMI_CONTRACT.md. Raising this further
 costs linearly in both; shortening the string fields is the lever if it matters.]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BaseType>INT</BaseType><Default><Value>128</Value></Default><Properties><Property><Name>TcVarGlobal</Name></Property></Properties><BitOffs>641633408</BitOffs></Symbol><Symbol><Name>PL_Fraktal.MAX_SEQUENCE_ANNOTATIONS</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §6.8 — chains attached to one Unit (incl. sub-chains)   // Core §3.2 / §8.2]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BaseType>INT</BaseType><Default><Value>16</Value></Default><Properties><Property><Name>TcVarGlobal</Name></Property></Properties><BitOffs>641633424</BitOffs></Symbol><Symbol><Name>PL_Fraktal.MAX_STEP_CONDS</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §6.9(b) condition records per step]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BaseType>INT</BaseType><Default><Value>8</Value></Default><Properties><Property><Name>TcVarGlobal</Name></Property></Properties><BitOffs>641633440</BitOffs></Symbol><Symbol><Name>PL_Fraktal.MAX_STATE_FLAGS</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §3.12 — derived state flags a module may publish. Statically sized
