 says so through PersistFailed instead of reverting silently at the next start.]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BaseType>UDINT</BaseType><Default><Value>5000</Value></Default><Properties><Property><Name>TcVarGlobal</Name></Property></Properties><BitOffs>641634112</BitOffs></Symbol><Symbol><Name>PL_Fraktal.MAX_PERSIST_DOC_BYTES</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §3.8b — one retained DOCUMENT on an I_PersistMedium: a rendered set (a
 header and MAX_SET_RECORDS lines of at most 480 characters fit) or the user
 table's image. Every FB_ConfigSetDocument holds one buffer of this size.]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BaseType>UDINT</BaseType><Default><Value>16384</Value></Default><Properties><Property><Name>TcVarGlobal</Name></Property></Properties><BitOffs>641634144</BitOffs></Symbol><Symbol><Name>PL_Fraktal.MAX_PERSIST_KEYS</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ documents a file medium vouches for (loss detection)]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BaseType>INT</BaseType><Default><Value>48</Value></Default><Properties><Property><Name>TcVarGlobal</Name></Property></Properties><BitOffs>641634176</BitOffs></Symbol><Symbol><Name>PL_Fraktal.MAX_RETAIN_DOCUMENTS</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ FB_RetainPersistMedium pool: 8 x 16 kB persistent]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BaseType>INT</BaseType><Default><Value>8</Value></Default><Properties><Property><Name>TcVarGlobal</Name></Property></Properties><BitOffs>641634192</BitOffs></Symbol><Symbol><Name>PL_Fraktal.MANUAL_HELD_REFRESH_MS</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §7.6.1a — how long a latched hold-to-run request survives without a
 refresh from the client. Long enough to ride out transport jitter, short
 enough that a closed HMI or a dead link lets go rather than leaving the
 machine moving. The module's own JogTimeout is the second, shorter net.]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BaseType>DWORD</BaseType><Default><Value>750</Value></Default><Properties><Property><Name>TcVarGlobal</Name></Property></Properties><BitOffs>641634208</BitOffs></Symbol><Symbol><Name>PL_Fraktal.CHART_REV_SETTLE_MS</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §3.13/§3.10.2 — how long the flow chart must stop growing before the
 manifest revision is raised for it.

 §3.13 rows are discovered by VISIT, one at a time, while the manifest is
 invalidated ALL AT ONCE. A per-row bump therefore asked a client to
 refetch the entire manifest once per row: entering AUTO on the press
 discovers 15 rows where HOME discovers 2, which is why HOME->AUTO stalled
 and HOME->HOME did not.

 Waiting for the burst to settle is strictly better than bumping per row,
 on BOTH counts: far fewer refetches, and the client fetches AFTER the
 chart stops growing rather than during it - which is the very failure the
 per-row bump was written to avoid ("a chart that grows after the HMI's
 fetch would render every new row with StepNo 0 and no text").]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BaseType>DWORD</BaseType><Default><Value>1000</Value></Default><Properties><Property><Name>TcVarGlobal</Name></Property></Properties><BitOffs>641634240</BitOffs></Symbol><Symbol><Name>PL_Fraktal.MAX_SAFETY_DEVICES</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §9 — published safety aliases per module/zone]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BaseType>INT</BaseType><Default><Value>16</Value></Default><Properties><Property><Name>TcVarGlobal</Name></Property></Properties><BitOffs>641634272</BitOffs></Symbol><Symbol><Name>PL_Fraktal.MAX_POWER_GROUPS</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §9 — independently controlled energy groups]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BaseType>INT</BaseType><Default><Value>8</Value></Default><Properties><Property><Name>TcVarGlobal</Name></Property></Properties><BitOffs>641634288</BitOffs></Symbol><Symbol><Name>PL_Fraktal.MAX_CONTROL_DOMAIN_UNITS</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §9.8 — root Units sharing one arrangement]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BaseType>INT</BaseType><Default><Value>16</Value></Default><Properties><Property><Name>TcVarGlobal</Name></Property></Properties><BitOffs>641634304</BitOffs></Symbol><Symbol><Name>PL_Fraktal.MAX_PARALLEL_BRANCHES</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §6.12 — concurrent legs one chain may run at once. It bounds the
